current_checkpoint_2026_08_24_canonical_companion_clean_gate_failure_and_fix_v1:
  authority: This is the newest first-read failure-preservation and red/green correction checkpoint. It does not overwrite or complete the preceding canonical companion checkpoint and grants no release, deployment, package, model, MemoryEndpoints, P2P, or campaign authority.
  remote_source: Companion commit `2abada7a3adb989ec8897205112d61c5a4d72477` was pushed and proven equal across local HEAD, tracking, FETCH_HEAD, and actual `ls-remote` before the gate.
  failed_gate: Fresh external evidence root `canonical-companion-clean-gate-20260824T022505Z` was proven absent before creation and direct/non-reparse. The maintained complete wrapper passed 1,052, failed one, and skipped one truthful missing-package-input case across 1,054 standard tests in 388,631.5713 ms. The failing real-Chromium test was `local web release smoke proves the exact closure in real Chromium`, failure code `BROWSER_SMOKE_FAILED`. Release shards did not start. Preserve the 737-byte bounded failure record SHA256 `12134eee50c7a2589e90b6f7d41260434f68524b77dec1d62d3c225794e21b50`; no retry was performed on that source/root.
  root_cause: The active web-release browser smoke still classified the companion as an install surface and required the exact NuGet link and install command. That contradicted the canonical unpublished-package rule and made the complete gate catch a real stale-contract defect.
  fix: Browser-smoke report identity advances incompatibly to `tinyrustlm.web_release_browser_smoke.v5`. The route class is `companion-release`; the page exposes exact `companionPackageStatus` and `companionDeploymentStatus` identities; the smoke requires `Public package pending` and `Deployment blocked`; it detects any UAIX Browser NuGet package link and any `dotnet add package` or `dotnet tool install` code and requires both absent. Testing documentation records this prepublication contract. No compatibility reader remains for report v4.
  verification: Focused real Chromium passes 1/1; the affected model-acquisition, browser-smoke, and local-Chromium union passes 12/12; complete UI passes 78/78. Run syntax, formatting, memory, diff, and secret checks before commit.
  exact_resume: Commit and push this fix, fetch, and prove remote equality. Create a different fresh external root proven absent and run the complete serial standard plus sharded release wrapper against the new clean commit. Never reuse or relabel the failed root. Only after a complete pass may the SLM2-only consumer replacement preregistration proceed.
  claim_boundary: MemoryEndpoints remains unauthorized and disconnected. Package `0.3.0` remains unbuilt and unpublished. Deployment remains blocked. Campaign counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20.

current_checkpoint_2026_08_24_canonical_companion_clean_slate_v1:
  authority: This is the newest first-read prelaunch companion, acquisition, package-source, browser, documentation, and no-legacy checkpoint. TinyRustLM has one current product contract. The companion now exposes only unversioned closed loopback routes; no versioned route family, protocol negotiation, compatibility header, alias, migration reader, fallback, or retained superseded executable behavior exists.
  source_control: The reviewed cutover is still an uncommitted coherent change over exact Prompt2 core commit `07120fa71a085f27fe64ba4e734db200082e1595` on branch `codex/model-acquisition-v2`. Commit it, push it, fetch it, and prove local HEAD, tracking ref, FETCH_HEAD, and actual `ls-remote` equality before a fresh complete clean-source release gate. The branch label is a source locator only. Modify only this recovered worktree; protected `E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com` remains untouched; never write `D:`.
  canonical_contract: Browser and SeedHost use only `/health`, `/pair`, `/status`, `/session/*`, `/imports/*`, `/conversions/*`, `/models/*`, and `/sharing/*`. `X-TinyRustLM-Bridge-Version`, protocol-version response fields, version middleware, and version errors are deleted. `/v0/health`, `/v1/health`, and `/v2/health` fail closed with `bridge_route_not_found`. Cross-tab identity is `tinyrustlm-companion-bridge`; state kind is `tinyrustlm.companion_state`; UI preference identity is `local-ai-dashboard`; conversion operation IDs use domain `TinyRustLM canonical bridge conversion`. No old-state, old-preference, old-operation-ID, or migration reader exists.
  coordinated_consumers: The browser bridge, C# server, JavaScript/C# tests, Playwright fixture and scenarios, ADR-004, package boundary tests, verification scripts, package docs, and both static HTML entry points moved together. Active acquisition test source is `tinyrustlm/tests/model-acquisition.test.js`; the superseded filename is removed. The narrow bridge HTTP stream fixture now carries `SLM2` magic. This does not convert the broader SeedHost fleet/import/admission harness, whose default remains the 8,832-byte SLM1 fixture. Campaign receipt public identifiers reject the former `[REDACTED]` reader marker instead of accepting it as legacy identity.
  package_boundary: Both SeedHost package projects target `0.3.0`, the first unused public semantic version after immutable `0.1.9` and `0.2.0` publication. Those packages are not yet published or independently read back. The source companion page truthfully shows `Public package pending` and `Deployment blocked`; the page, repository README, and package guide expose no dead `0.3.0` NuGet link or install command. Matching install assets must not appear or deploy until both NuGet packages and symbol packages pass SLM2-only build, clean-consumer verification, publication, and immutable public readback. No local package creation is publication evidence.
  remaining_slm1_blocker: A broader executable-path scan still finds the superseded SLM1 runtime/packer in `tinyrustlm/runtime`, `tinyrustlm/tools/slm_pack`, and related current workspace membership. This companion checkpoint does not hide or authorize it. Package `0.3.0`, product deployment, and the first real-model release remain blocked until a preregistered SLM2 consumer closure explicitly supersedes frozen root-Cargo evidence, moves the browser/package/converter path to the sole SLM2 implementation, removes SLM1 workspace membership and executable source, rewrites current docs/tests/fixtures, and passes the complete gates. Research intake and immutable historical evidence may retain the text `SLM1` only as non-executable history.
  verification: Focused campaign-evidence, companion, and acquisition Node tests pass 26/26; focused SeedHost HTTP tests pass 10/10; package-boundary tests pass 2/2; `dotnet format --verify-no-changes`, JavaScript syntax, and diff hygiene pass; complete UI tests pass 78/78; complete package tests pass 68/68; complete Core tests pass 75/75. Real-Chromium UI report run `20260824T0141182802144Z-c7f6db090736` passes at 10,119 bytes and SHA256 `064fbab9e4f8247916c65a37715d53b2a20000e2a75791927521e94455229d4b`. Deep acquisition run `20260824T0145171177628Z-35120196d1fa` passes static, syntax, browser contracts, real Chromium, browser bridge, SeedHost 53/53, and the old SLM1 `tinyrustlm-slm-pack` converter 7/7. Its 14,675-byte report SHA256 is `efa5d40858812b1a8e19b5e1517800a18cb65a4de5bea4e6b9dfc43d902d862d` and nested browser report SHA256 is `6f5f27720337ec9ae810ae6ad77fc4fe28b7664edd9fc9c595f3e3be8b1323ad`. This is legacy-path diagnostic evidence only, never SLM2 product proof.
