  preserved_failures: The first fuzz compile rejected consuming `Unstructured::take_rest` through a mutable borrow; the exact remaining bytes are now read without moving the value. The first fuzz Clippy gate rejected three needless borrows; they were removed without suppression. The first independent Node contract run passed 0/3, and the first four-file affected run passed 25/27, because older tests derived root authority from a junction-resolved `__dirname`. One strict shared test-root authority now prefers explicit `TINYRUSTLM_REPOSITORY_ROOT`, requires one complete absolute root, and removes that topology ambiguity; the corrected runs are the 3/3 and 27/27 evidence above. None of the first failures is rewritten as a product pass or parser regression.
