  canonicalizer_contract: One BCL-only `TinyRustLM.PackageCanonicalizer` executable is a first-class solution project and the sole implementation used by both pack scripts. It requires absolute unsigned `.nupkg` or `.snupkg` files; rejects a reparse file or direct parent, signed archives, traversal, backslashes, nonportable names, Windows device names, portable duplicates, and bounded entry/name/compressed/uncompressed/package-size violations; streams SHA-256; writes one exclusive same-directory temporary; assigns `1980-01-01T00:00:00Z`; verifies ordered entry names, lengths, compressed lengths, attributes, and decompressed hashes; flushes; promotes only after equivalence; and performs final readback. Already canonical bytes are not rewritten. No shell-specific ZIP rewrite, migration reader, or compatibility path exists.
  audit_contract: Package audit is a clean cut to `tinyrustlm.nuget.package_audit.v1`. It records the canonical timestamp plus main and symbol noncanonical-entry inventories/counts and fails on any drift. Maintained publish readers accept v1 only. A source regression extracts and compares the complete PowerShell/Bash public API literal sets instead of pinning one constructor by hand.
  preserved_failure_history:
    storage_red: The first red test command failed before assertions because E: filled. Its immutable transcript is `D:\TinyRustLM-vnext-20260812\test-logs\package-canonicalizer-red.log`, SHA256 `5bd39f2b45ac9e59779c6fa164291a797c35626bb0a7822bc087e63bc9bf7e1d`. Only generated active `bin`/`obj` output from that run was removed after resolved-path verification.
    root_locator: The first complete package-test run passed 57 tests and failed nine topology-sensitive root-locator cases. That nonzero transcript is `package-tests-v1-active.log`, SHA256 `d03e6b9d4ba85c9f1ee282cb758a9f2a275ebe76f6bb3eafa6ba63aea9d3d608`; the general `TINYRUSTLM_REPO_ROOT` repair then passed 66/66 in `package-tests-v1-active-rerun.log`, SHA256 `4e42e7ccb505d2ea4cc63fa7dfa6d217350e13fc124d16f18f4c7bda464525da`.
    verifier_wrappers: One first wrapper timed out after one second without a usable transcript. A second wrapper incorrectly treated normal Cargo stderr as terminating under `ErrorActionPreference=Stop`; preserve `verify-package-9e60539-generation-1.log`, SHA256 `c9211c652b556278514fd3e2acd9a9dfe3ca78f49b0ae87e976d14401f6e18e8`. Neither is counted as product failure or passing evidence.
    retained_feed: Audit v1 over the preserved pre-canonical package feed remains a truthful fail: 13 documentation-byte mismatches, 38 main timestamp findings, 20 symbol timestamp findings, and two requested-but-absent native RIDs. Report SHA256 is `d2a5d05f62abe90208b90fb69a448ac6ebfa98bdce7fe2c2e350733ac727ad01`; it was not overwritten or converted into a pass.
    bash_runtime_parity: The first Bash audit over canonical packages failed because all-RID input exceeded the local `win-x64` package scope and one Bash constructor literal omitted a trailing `System.Int32`. Its report remains at `D:\tw\3116220\artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-nuget-package-audit-bash.json`, SHA256 `e8cd2d22cb654e61c3fe622bcff35d314c46a2d0206a8ff28c6b852beffcbbd8`; it is retained as a nonzero predecessor and is not the current positive audit.
  verification:
    focused: Canonicalizer unit tests pass 11/11; focused integration passes 15/15. The current complete package project passes 67/67 at `7cc3579`; stdout SHA256 is `648619727c9ae374d131c07e622bd7f475e2f4b22b187b0665fcb920d6e17793` and stderr is empty.
    complete_generation_1: The physical complete verifier at source `9e60539` exited zero and covered Rust, Core 75/75, Package 66/66, SeedHost 50/50, canonicalization of eight packages, audit v1, and the isolated consumer. Stdout SHA256 is `176f47c39fa5402bd8ce6686fdcab627964d6540c558782c4e652a6ba9d71c7f`; stderr SHA256 is `aa532ba6515bebb05e13caa7b5df32335b9b2d5ec7da02c76677494061deefe5`.
