  implemented_scope:
    - Replaced the single-directory helper request with the sole closed batch protocol. It accepts 1 through 1024 sorted unique operation identities in at most 4 MiB and returns one complete path-redacted observation or one bounded failure document. The retired single-request and single-observation schemas are absent from maintained sources.
    - Added `flushMany` as the production Node boundary with one helper process per batch; `flush` is only its size-one API wrapper. Package, executable, profile, request, observation, process, path, and source-closure identities remain exact and no caller may inject success.
    - Added `publishMany` with complete preflight, deterministic target order, one target-directory flush batch, exact target readback, one receipt-directory flush batch, exact receipt readback, and activation only after the complete set succeeds. It returns no partial API success but explicitly does not claim transactional filesystem mutation; inactive files may remain as preserved evidence.
    - Added receipt-store `putMany` with exact wire and identity validation, aggregate capacity preflight, active-or-same-batch parent closure, deterministic topological order, cycle rejection, fresh external closure validation, one durable batch publication, and all-or-none activation. `put` is the size-one wrapper.
    - Added subject-store `putMany` with exact closed-array validation, unique identities, aggregate capacity preflight, one durable batch publication, and activation only after complete success. Campaign fixtures now persist receipt and subject sets through those batch APIs.
    - Added one repeatable campaign-release-surface gate runner. It freezes six nonoverlapping shards that cover all 23 exact test names once, validates the partition before execution, starts independent no-shell Node processes, bounds and terminates process trees, and retains the original test bodies and thresholds.
    - Normalized ADR-012 into the mandatory accepted ADR shape and closed ADR-001 through ADR-012 inventory. The decision records batch semantics, nonrecursive durability bootstrap, explicit nonclaims, archive-custody unknowns, clean deletion, and forward-only rollback.
