    protected_checkout: E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com remains heavily dirty with unrelated user work and must not be edited, reset, cleaned, reverted, or used for this branch.
  implemented_scope:
    - Added the isolated `tinyrustlm-durability` workspace crate and sole `tinyrustlm-directory-flush` host process. The crate forbids unsafe Rust and has no network dependency or alternate implementation path.
    - Frozen one current 16,384-byte bounded stdin JSON protocol. Strict Serde parsing rejects duplicate, unknown, malformed, oversized, and wrong-schema requests. Success returns one path-redacted observation; failure returns only schema, status, and one declared bounded code.
    - Owned-path validation requires an absolute UTF-8 root, one-to-64 normal relative components, canonical containment, no symbolic-link or Windows reparse component, and pre-open, opened-handle, and post-flush metadata inspection.
    - Windows opens the directory with `GENERIC_WRITE`, all three share modes, `FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS`, and `FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT`, then requires `File::sync_all` success. Unix uses read-open plus directory `sync_all`; other platforms fail closed.
    - Caller-held single-writer ownership is an explicit precondition because stable Rust 1.96 file-index and volume-serial access is experimental. The helper does not silently claim to defeat an independent concurrent writer.
    - The Win64 host executed the actual directory flush path. A real Windows directory junction was created and rejected as `directory_path_link`. These are local API observations only.
    - Corrected the repository ignore policy so normal Git staging includes every Rust `src/bin` source file even though generated `bin` directories remain ignored.
    - Contract README, architecture inventory, threat review, dedicated durability documentation, Cargo workspace metadata, private file handoff, and lockfile were updated in the same checkpoint.
