    truth_and_verification_rule: Distinguish research, proposal, implementation, local test, independent proof, deployment, rejection, blocker, and unavailable behavior. Verify runnable examples, links, navigation, search discoverability, accessibility, responsive rendering, API/schema references, version agreement, and public HTTPS readback before publication.
    release_gate: An affected product, catalog, marketing, redirect, or documentation site is not publishable while its documentation is incomplete, stale, contradictory, version-skewed, unverified, or inconsistent with implementation and release evidence.
    commit_cadence: Commit and push every coherent major change as soon as its affected build and checks are healthy. Do not hold a valid checkpoint for unrelated future perfection.
    deployment_cadence: Publish each affected site promptly when its complete affected release gate passes. Internal-only changes with no deployable site-byte delta still require commit and push but do not fabricate a new site release. Preserve any failing gate as a blocker.
