    phase_3_rust_signature_primitive_parity_checkpoint:
      status: Commit `bbcc89053e1f431a716af95ff3a733338d7f3009` is pushed and remote-exact. It independently derives the frozen canonical signature payload, domain-separated signing bytes, strict Ed25519 verification result, and stable primitive rejection codes in Rust for native and `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. It is primitive parity only, not authority-graph evaluation, registry succession, revocation or compromise handling, nonce-replay state, offline-bundle closure, trusted production time or key custody, release authorization, Phase 3 completion, a site release, or live campaign evidence.
      implementation_scope: `rust/crates/tinyrustlm-evidence/src/signature.rs` accepts one complete canonical signature-envelope wire and one canonical raw 32-byte public key. It independently enforces exact algorithm, role/domain, scope, safe-ID, content-ID, signed-schema, hash, UTC, expiry, lifetime, canonical base64, payload-hash, and strict Ed25519 invariants. The canonical payload has exactly 14 signed fields, and signing bytes are `UTF8(signatureDomain) || 0x00 || canonical payload`. The public API returns owned immutable payload, signing, and result bytes plus exact lowercase SHA-256 values or one bounded stable error code. It performs no filesystem, network, process, clock, environment, retry, repair, key generation, authority discovery, or best-result behavior.
