    phase_3_rust_offline_bundle_parity_checkpoint:
      status: Commit `fee4d802f2b6c6477e24f6c341a1e2e63382776e` is pushed and remote-exact. It independently reproduces the frozen complete offline-verification-bundle decision in strict Rust for native and `wasm32-unknown-unknown`, returning the exact canonical Node result bytes and stable rejection codes. It is offline verification only, not truthful campaign projection, browser currentness execution, a production campaign runner, production key or trusted-time custody, a site release, Phase 3 completion, or live campaign evidence.
      implementation_scope: `rust/crates/tinyrustlm-evidence/src/offline_bundle.rs` composes the completed strict receipt, six-family subject, Ed25519 primitive, and authority-graph boundaries. It enforces caller-pinned manifest hash, campaign, environment, root registry, terminal registry, and verification time; exact frozen profile and schema bindings; canonical manifest bytes; bounded receipt and subject collections; exact member hashes and metadata; separate verification-receipt binding; complete receipt categories and parents; terminal-registry currentness; target current-evidence eligibility; recursive dependency, supersession, attestation, registry, revocation, signature, and nested-offline parents; and exact closed membership with no omitted, surplus, recursive, duplicate, substituted, or unlinked member. The API performs no filesystem, network, process, environment, clock discovery, key generation, signing, retry, repair, compatibility, or projection behavior.
      frozen_vectors: `contracts/vnext/offline-bundle-rust-vectors.v1.json` is 658,110 bytes with SHA-256 `c50a9668725a67df15f45fd28c4c80addde89e53fe80468590005a9fcb293ba8`. It binds profile `tinyrustlm.vnext.offline-bundle.v1`, whose exact SHA-256 is `62e37b24391ce48cc8be71184e71a67ebd0972e90dca79cf8036099091349e9f`, and public authority seed SHA-256 `c078e980fd1c633d4c46b8dddf3d25fc3f9bc5a11f1d5f940c6df7db08e72ab7`. Three accepted bundles freeze byte-identical Node/Rust canonical results and hashes. Thirty-one hostile cases require exact shared stable error codes for input and resource bounds, manifest shape/profile/hash/canonicality/pins/times/totals, member omission/surplus/duplication/hash/metadata/campaign drift, recursive verification receipts, verification-receipt binding/category/parent errors, authority failures, stale terminal or target evidence, governance signature errors, incomplete closure, and unlinked receipts or subjects.
      public_only_generation: `tinyrustlm/tools/vnext-offline-bundle-rust-vectors.js` derives the corpus only from the frozen public authority seed and installed public profiles. It generates no key, signs no payload, reads no clock or environment, accesses no network, and reproduces the checked-in corpus byte-for-byte. Checked-in seed and vectors contain public keys and signatures but no private key material.
      verification: The focused `tinyrustlm-evidence` crate passed 28 unit and integration tests, including all three accepted offline bundles and all 31 exact rejections. Focused Node offline, authority, and signature documentation/replay checks passed. Repository rustfmt, denied-warning all-target workspace Clippy, and the locked/offline `wasm32-unknown-unknown` evidence build passed. The complete locked/offline Rust workspace passed with zero failures, and complete `npm run test:unit` passed 811/811 with zero failures and zero skipped in 67.9 seconds, including real Chromium fault, generated plan-WASM, and local web-release smoke coverage. Deterministic regeneration retained corpus hash `c50a9668725a67df15f45fd28c4c80addde89e53fe80468590005a9fcb293ba8`; JavaScript syntax, staged diff, ASCII, NUL, dependency/lockfile, compatibility-denial, private-path, and secret-pattern reviews passed.
      documentation: `docs/architecture/vnext-rust-offline-bundle-parity.md` defines and test-binds the exact boundary and non-claims. The offline-bundle architecture, signature-authority architecture, Rust primitive and authority records, contract inventory, and contract README were updated together. A full-suite failure caused by a stale assertion was retained, corrected to require completed offline parity and incomplete truthful projection, and rerun through all 811 tests.
      deployment_truth: Zero of the 23 production deployment-manifest members changed. Publishing unchanged bytes would fabricate a release, so no deployment, version increment, Updates entry, release receipt, or public readback claim was created. The implementation, public corpus, tests, and architecture documentation were committed and pushed immediately after all complete affected gates passed.
      campaign_truth: Live progress remains 0/20 qualifying models, 0/50 deletion-backed clean-browser rounds, 0/25 authorized live memory rounds, 0/40 outside-network lane proofs, and 0/20 catalog announcements.
      exact_resume_boundary: Freeze one deterministic cross-language truthful-projection corpus from exact plan, currentness, authority, and offline-bundle inputs. Begin with failing Rust tests for byte-identical accepted projections and stable rejection codes covering honest zeros, complete capacity, stale and superseded evidence, duplicate objective evidence, no-double-counting, unsigned or unplanned inputs, expired outside proofs, explicit blockers, limits, and final completion. Implement the projection independently in Rust without invoking Node or importing verdict outputs. Then extend the one generated WASM/browser transport to currentness and projection bytes without handwritten browser semantics or a second ABI.
    phase_3_rust_truthful_projection_parity_checkpoint:
      status: Commits `2d2e704` (`test(evidence): freeze campaign projection parity vectors`) and `4ad96fed6e369dc3ac4a557220d19a15ca9df15d` (`feat(evidence): add Rust campaign projection parity`) are pushed and remote-exact. Together they freeze one deterministic public-only cross-language corpus and independently reproduce the truthful campaign projection decision in strict Rust for native and `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. This is not browser currentness/projection execution, a production runner, a release, Phase 3 completion, or live campaign evidence.
      projection_boundary: Projection independently revalidates the exact plan, canonical receipt and subject collections, semantic-currentness result, and signature-authority graph before objective counting. Offline-bundle verification is a separate closed-membership decision and is intentionally not accepted as projection input. Qualification, browser, memory, outside-proof, and catalog objectives retain exact plan membership, dependency, currentness, authority-role, identity-distinctness, no-double-counting, blocker, honest-zero, resumability, and completion semantics.
      rust_api: `project_campaign`, `validate_campaign_projection_result`, `CampaignProjectionInput`, `CampaignProjectionError`, `VerifiedCampaignProjection`, `CAMPAIGN_PROJECTION_PROFILE_SHA256`, and `CAMPAIGN_PROJECTION_RESULT_SCHEMA` expose owned canonical result bytes and stable bounded errors. `rust/crates/tinyrustlm-evidence/src/projection.rs` contains no filesystem, network, clock, environment, process, retry, repair, compatibility, best-result selection, `unwrap`, `expect`, panic, or unreachable production path.
      frozen_public_corpus: `contracts/vnext/campaign-projection-public-seed.v1.json` is 1,024,171 bytes with SHA-256 `1c908cd4238167c4b16bde0a65246c08f220b5a0d73937d31747344608c52234`. `contracts/vnext/campaign-projection-rust-vectors.v1.json` is 1,494,464 bytes with SHA-256 `974396d30525b6fc62e568de72361b99e87a99b6e33ead2e5cb43cfa002ec8a6`; it contains 277 public receipts and 41 public subjects, 11 accepted projections, 22 exact input rejections, and 8 exact projection-result wire rejections. The deterministic generator reads public frozen inputs, generates no keys or signatures, uses no private material, clock, environment, or network, and reproduces the corpus byte-for-byte.
      hostile_coverage: Exact parity covers honest zero, partial and complete progress, explicit blockers, stale or superseded evidence withdrawal, unresolved currentness conflicts, duplicate and unplanned evidence, no-double-counting, unsigned evidence, source/dependency mismatch, expired outside proof, missing authority pins and terminal registry, malformed or oversized receipt and subject collections, phase-parent graph defects, profile drift, and malformed, noncanonical, inconsistent, or trailing projection-result wire.
      verification: The focused original-plus-vector Node projection set passed 15/15. The complete locked/offline `tinyrustlm-evidence` all-target set passed 32 unit and integration tests with zero failures. Repository Rust formatting, denied-warning all-target evidence Clippy, deterministic generation, JavaScript syntax, exact size/hash assertions, diff checks, NUL checks, and bounded private-material scans passed before each commit. One eager optional-index defect found by accepted parity was preserved as a failing result and corrected with an explicit branch before the complete rerun.
      documentation: `docs/architecture/vnext-rust-campaign-projection-parity.md` is the detailed authority for this boundary. Campaign projection, plan parity, offline-bundle parity, signature authority, contract inventory, contract README, and exact vector tests are updated together and explicitly preserve the separation between closed offline membership and truthful projection.
      deployment_truth: Zero of the 23 production deployment-manifest members changed. Publishing unchanged bytes would fabricate a release, so no deployment, version increment, Updates entry, release receipt, or public readback claim was created. The corpus and implementation were committed and pushed as separate coherent checkpoints as soon as their affected gates passed.
