      ownership_and_state: Rust records exact pointer-length allocations before copy/release, returns no borrowed pointers, owns staged copies, rejects over-count and over-aggregate appends before commit, and destroys stage/result/error on begin, protocol or resource failure, execute, and reset. Projection accepts exact raw plan, receipt, subject, caller pin, and caller time bytes and independently revalidates them. Offline-bundle verification remains a separate closed-membership decision and is not accepted as projection input.
      browser_evidence: Node and two independently created real Chromium persistent profiles reproduce exact plan, phase-currentness, honest-zero, nonzero projection, result validation, and stable rejection bytes. Both profiles close and are physically deleted with distinct deletion identities; both runs make zero requests and emit zero page or console errors. These profiles prove verifier conformance only and do not count among the 50 campaign rounds.
