    phase_3_campaign_runner_checkpoint:
      status: Commit `386f643d95a0b67f1e695de27f5813b9b2108050` (`feat(evidence): add exact Rust-backed campaign runner`) is pushed, clean, and remote-exact. It implements the sole local cross-store campaign projection runner and immutable operation history. It is not operational entry-point cutover, final attestation or release authorization, a production durability claim, live campaign evidence, a release, a deployment, or Phase 3 completion.
      frozen_profile: `contracts/vnext/campaign-runner-profile.v1.json` is 6,855 bytes with SHA-256 `77e75dd7a4f04e23421be740040ea52efe68c234f49377005d94c550b9c142e7`. It binds the exact receipt, public-subject, campaign-artifact, and generated campaign-evidence profiles; all-member selection; caller-trusted verification time; two complete observations; create-only operation history; finite resource limits; no network, environment, caller-verdict, best-of-N, stored-result-currentness, or mutable-pointer path; and one incompatible no-compatibility policy.
      exact_snapshot_and_projection: Every operation rebuilds the exact plan, receipt store, and public-subject store twice; reads every sorted active member; copies and hashes exact bytes; binds member IDs, wire hashes, byte lengths, aggregate bytes, and profile identities; and rejects any cross-observation drift. The second owned observation is sent only to the generated Rust campaign-evidence ABI. Rust independently validates the returned projection before the create-only campaign-artifact store persists it. Restart always resnapshots and reprojects; surviving projection bytes are reusable only when exact content identity matches and never become a currentness pointer.
      immutable_operation_history: Domain-separated canonical start records bind operation ID, plan identity, campaign/environment pins, authority pins, trusted time, exact receipt and subject snapshots, profile IDs, and WASM module identity. A completed terminal binds the exact persisted projection SHA-256; a failed terminal carries only bounded error code and step. Start precedes projection, terminal follows projection persistence, start without terminal is interrupted, byte-identical interruption resume is permitted, terminal operation reuse and conflicting history fail closed, and rejected or obsolete records are never overwritten.
      append_only_process_exclusion: Locking uses immutable monotonic generation claims plus create-only identity-bound releases. Each claim binds generation, random nonce, process ID, predecessor-claim hash, reason, and schema. A live or indeterminate latest owner returns `campaign_runner_busy`; a released or provably dead latest owner permits contenders to race on exactly one next-generation hard-link target, electing one winner without deleting, renaming, or quarantining any claim or release. This removes the stale-lock check-delete-create race; PID reuse remains a safe false-busy condition.
      hostile_and_failure_coverage: Tests cover hostile option accessors, overlapping roots, WASM substitution, honest zero, trusted-time restart withdrawal, duplicate signature no-double-counting, superseded pass withdrawal, exact 271-receipt/40-subject synthetic capacity, cross-store mutation, bounded Rust failure, real process death after start publication, immutable stale-generation recovery, two real processes racing the same dead generation with exactly one winner, a live concurrent holder, disk-full start persistence, and exact canonical operation identity.
