      clean_truth_boundary: `vnext-campaign-release-surface.js` constructs the sole campaign runner internally and accepts no stored projection, caller counter, dashboard verdict, attestation payload, or status override. A never-before-used operation ID is mandatory. The surface executes and validates a fresh exact runner result, binds operation, plan, projection, campaign, environment, authority, trusted-time, start, terminal, and snapshot identities, and rejects absent, reused, failed, interrupted, or mismatched operation truth.
      immutable_output_and_redaction: A complete-or-blocked final-attestation receipt is content-addressed and written only through the bounded create-only public-subject store. Canonical attestation bytes are checked against the protected known-secret equality list before persistence. A scan failure persists only a public-safe redaction receipt and returns no unsafe attestation bytes. Operator status is derived from the attestation and can only be `campaign-incomplete`, `campaign-complete-awaiting-release-inputs`, or `release-evidence-redaction-blocked`; there is no caller-supplied or generic `done` state.
      frozen_profile: `contracts/vnext/campaign-release-surface-profile.v1.json` has SHA-256 `a798083041c9cfd824c27625719f6313a4f3ef48bb0d457a81b027194360486a`. The profile, implementation, tests, architecture account, contract registry guidance, runner/inventory/threat documentation, package command, and maintained TinyRustLM testing/browser/runtime documentation were updated together.
      verification: The focused surface suite passed 7/7. The adjacent runner, projection, receipt-store, and redaction set passed 65/65. Registry, inventory, and threat-review tests passed 12/12. The complete JavaScript unit gate passed 844/844 with zero failures and zero skipped in 68.6 seconds. Final source hardening was followed by another 7/7 focused pass. JavaScript syntax, strict JSON parsing, `git diff --check`, staged ASCII/NUL checks, bounded secret/private-key/private-path scans, stale-stack import checks, and production-manifest intersection checks passed.
      documentation_and_deployment_truth: Exactly zero of the 23 TinyRustLM production deployment-manifest members changed. Publishing unchanged site bytes would fabricate a release, so no site version, Updates entry, deployment, release receipt, public readback claim, or campaign counter was created. The coherent code and documentation checkpoint was committed and pushed immediately after its affected gates passed.
