      exact_resume_boundary: Extend this same sole surface with release-manifest v2 preparation over current approved claim.v2, artifact, package, SBOM, provenance, changelog, and remaining-risk inputs from the fresh runner snapshot; verify the current release-authorizer signature through the vNext authority graph; add strict HTTPS exact-byte readback, deployment, published-claim, and site-publisher descendants. Then switch every maintained entry point and delete the superseded mutable release stack in the same verified replacement.
    phase_3_public_release_text_scanner_checkpoint:
      status: Commit `af99ffa4a6e45babcffb184e974fda6b20d71f1d` (`feat(evidence): scan canonical public release text`) is pushed and remote-exact. It adds the bounded public-text prerequisite for release changelogs to the existing private-by-default redaction boundary. It is not release-manifest preparation, release authorization, deployment, publication, a campaign receipt, or Phase 3 completion.
      canonical_text_boundary: `scanVnextPublicTextBytes` accepts copied bounded byte views only, requires fatal UTF-8 with no BOM, CR, NUL, DEL, disallowed C0 controls, or missing terminal LF, derives a domain-separated identity over exact bytes, and applies the existing known-secret representation, contextual credential/private-path/raw-content, and entropy detectors. It returns an unchanged defensive byte copy only on pass and returns no source bytes on failure. Receipt replay must name exactly `document` or `public-text`; omission, an unknown kind, or kind confusion fails closed, and no compatibility reader accepts the prior verifier input shape.
      frozen_facts: `contracts/vnext/public-safe-redaction-profile.v1.json` is 3,473 bytes with SHA-256 `83fcdd3590692304807e1ca62f82ad5873111cf0cce6b239bd51249d5c29d2b0`. The transitively pinned campaign-release-surface profile is 3,419 bytes with SHA-256 `53a31b50560ee12c122dc00bc396893788380dc4ddc200ecabf194ed69264541`. The regenerated public-only Rust offline-bundle corpus is 658,110 bytes with SHA-256 `53d619c4ca4fcf1f1effe6f8678327cdeebd95c8953843da342e6374dcc9bf26`.
