    phase_3_release_authorization_checkpoint:
      status: Code commit `ac0b9abc8137127775924732f64d1cd453ca4dbb` (`feat(evidence): verify release authorization`) is pushed and remote-exact. It extends the sole release surface with current vNext Ed25519 release-authorizer verification as a forward-only child of the prepared manifest. The documentation and redaction-only interruption regression in this containing checkpoint were verified after that code commit. This is not deployment, public readback, publication, live campaign evidence, or Phase 3 completion.
      authorization_truth_boundary: `authorizeRelease` accepts one closed data-only input: canonical authorization receipt bytes, canonical changelog bytes, exact prepared manifest ID, campaign/environment/source pins, trusted verification time, caller-pinned authority root and terminal, and the bounded protected equality list. It accepts no decision, verdict, status, deployment, publication, counter, stored projection, or mutable current pointer. It reconstructs the exact final attestation, runner start and terminal records, complete Rust-backed projection, original receipt and subject snapshots, selected release evidence, claims, and three preparation scans from create-only storage before authorization can be considered.
      authority_and_identity: The sole admitted authorization is one canonical `signature-envelope` receipt with role `release-authorizer`, domain `tinyrustlm.signature.release-authorizer.v1`, scope `release-authorization`, signed schema `tinyrustlm.vnext.release_manifest.v2`, exact manifest subject and release ID, exact canonical-content hash, matching campaign and source revision, and a finite current lifetime. The full vNext authority graph must verify under the caller-pinned root and terminal; signature validity, authority at issue, temporal currentness, current-evidence eligibility, empty stale reasons, and terminal-registry currentness are all mandatory. Retired, revoked, compromised, expired, duplicate, wrong-role, wrong-scope, wrong-release, drifted, or caller-decided evidence fails closed.
      redaction_persistence_and_restart: Preparation scans are replayed against the current protected list. Authorization bytes are scanned before persistence; unsafe bytes leave only one bounded public-safe failure scan. On success, the deterministic authorization-redaction receipt is create-only persisted before the signature receipt. Exact membership admits only prepared, prepared-plus-redaction, or prepared-plus-redaction-plus-signature states, proving restart recovery after the first write and byte-identical full replay. The immutable prepared manifest is never mutated. Success returns only `release-authorized-awaiting-deployment` and no `done`, deployed, published, or counter claim.
