    phase_3_deployment_attempt_admission_checkpoint:
      status: This containing source-controlled checkpoint extends only the sole r5/v3 campaign release surface with immutable deployment-attempt admission. It is not deployment success, production HTTPS readback, publication, live campaign evidence, or Phase 3 completion.
      deployment_truth_boundary: `admitDeploymentAttempt` accepts one closed data-only input over an existing prepared and authorized release. It reconstructs the exact runner operation, projection, receipt and subject snapshots, release evidence, preparation scans, stored release-authorizer signature, and its redaction receipt; then reruns the current authority graph at deployment verification time. It accepts no deployed, succeeded, published, done, readback, counter, caller verdict, mutable pointer, or fixture truth.
      exact_attempt_contract: The only admitted child is one canonical `deployment` receipt with phase/type `deployment`, status `pass`, runtime execution class `deployment`, and mandatory scope `deployment-attempt-only`. Here `pass` authenticates only the bounded attempt record, never the remote result. The current web build is its sole phase dependency; the campaign attestation uses the dedicated attestation field; and release authorization is an exact receipt reference plus public parameter, so deployment remains classifiable by the closed phase-currentness graph. The receipt also binds the release-manifest canonical hash, r5/v3 static inventory identity, deployment manifest, publication generator, security-header profile, public HTTPS origin, asset count, total bytes, submitted inventory, and one bounded transcript digest. Its attempt begins after stored authorization admission and completes no later than trusted verification time.
      redaction_persistence_and_replay: The final canonical attempt receipt is scanned against the same protected equality set used throughout preparation. On pass, its deterministic redaction receipt is create-only persisted before the deployment receipt. The only admitted store states are exact-authorized, exact-authorized-plus-redaction, and exact-authorized-plus-redaction-plus-deployment; byte-identical replay recovers either write. Unsafe deployment bytes persist only the bounded failed redaction receipt and never the deployment receipt. Any unrelated active receipt or subject blocks admission.
