    - This session is not connected to MemoryEndpoints.com; the authoritative production single-use enrollment/reconnect/cleanup contract and authorized disposable-company credentials are unavailable, so live continuity remains 0/25.
    - No authorized independent outside-network observer and current signed complete-transfer receipts exist for 40 public lanes, so outside proof remains 0/40 and catalog announcement remains 0/20.
    - Required real-hardware execution evidence, including physical `linux-arm64`, remains distinct from cross-compilation, binary inspection, or emulation and is not complete.
    - Role-separated campaign evidence keys, trust registry, publication authorization, and all non-TinyRustLM site release ledgers must be provisioned and verified before their corresponding claims can close.
    - MiniModel.org `master` has a pre-existing release-gate defect: its full Rust workspace run reaches tests but fails 21 `minimodel-core` cases because checked-in peer-offer proof hashes differ from admission hashes; its Node catalog set passes 11/12 and fails the published announcement-feed hash binding. The documentation-policy commit is isolated from those inputs, but MiniModel publication remains blocked until the defects are repaired and the full gate passes.
    - Runtime.MiRust.com's PowerShell verifier throws an `Invoke-WebRequest` null-reference on its first HEAD request under the installed Windows PowerShell. Independent `curl` observed the intended `301` to the developer portal and subsequent `200`, but that does not repair the verifier. PHP is unavailable locally, so PHP syntax validation was not executed. Runtime publication remains blocked on a working verifier and complete release gate.
    - The current `PLUTO\AI` process cannot write the six existing `E:\Source\Rust\{site}\.uai\totem.uai` files because those checkouts grant write access to other Windows identities only. Remote policy commits are authoritative and exact; protected local checkouts remain stale until their owner updates permissions or refreshes them. Do not delete or replace those files to bypass the ACL.
  related_site_account:
    inventory_scope: Direct site roots under `E:\Source\Rust`; current routing lives in the mutable `E:\Source\Rust\workspace.uai`, while the bounded public observations below are dated 2026-08-09. A live response, source commit, package version, HTTP Last-Modified value, and immutable publication receipt are different evidence classes and are labeled separately below.
    LMComposer.com: Retired alias. Private repository `MichaelKappel/LMComposer.com` on `main` now contains the complete bounded redirect package, tests, version/update metadata, totem, taboo, and restart memory at pushed head `36d6389fe82b0f53c4d8951aa6af5cb896fd8bf6`. Production responds with a redirect to TinyRustLM.com. Last publication remains unknown because no immutable site release ledger exists; source control is complete but deployment is unclaimed.
    MiniModel.MiRust.com: Active documentation-first MiniModel developer and protocol reference. Remote `master` is policy commit `f462195e7af2b08f08edcd190d848560495cd287`; the protected local checkout remains at `3c5f9e28c48fd2b843f58df91accc5579a3270a5` until its owner refreshes it. The prior observed live root was byte-identical to that older local commit and returned Last-Modified `2026-07-12T22:33:49Z`; this is not publication authority and the new policy commit is not claimed deployed.
    MiniModel.org: Active catalog and direct-P2P discovery surface with required user, developer, and operator documentation; it must never proxy model bytes. Remote `master` is policy commit `6718981631e6e6a5efcd9b5d44216d1cfc6c4083`; the protected local checkout remains at `693c50f0fa2a82fd502dfc9d38c0e140531850da`. Full Rust and Node gates expose the recorded pre-existing hash-drift failures, so publication is blocked and the policy commit is not claimed deployed.
    MiRust.com: Active documentation, evidence, marketing, architecture, research, and governance authority. Remote `master` is policy commit `b3dcbb90337d3e19a3da09c9b575aa5cc963c09b`; the protected local checkout remains at `6dd665033c1d3a8ef907ee3140707a6fcb4c0357`. The live footer still reports latest content update `2026-06-25T16:42:00Z` and Theme/Core `2.3.0`; no new deployment is claimed and no immutable release ledger exists.
    Runtime.MiRust.com: Retired redirect with bounded historical evidence, currently routing to `https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/developer-portal/`. Remote `master` is policy commit `8cb141dc9c0387c5fcf37e6f7dbc9af83352fa6e`; the protected local checkout remains at `3bf5a5de50d21c4a10e8dd08dffa1eabd83199fc`. Independent HTTPS observation found the expected `301` then `200`, but the declared verifier is defective and no deployment or immutable publication is claimed.
    TinyRustLM.com: Active browser-local product surface. Code commit `af99ffa4a6e45babcffb184e974fda6b20d71f1d` is pushed and remote-exact on `codex/model-acquisition-v2`; it adds canonical public release-text scanning and transitive Node/Rust parity while changing zero production deployment-manifest members. The current immutable ledger still records only `tinyrustlm.com@0.2.1`, release date `2026-08-08`, published `2026-08-08T23:47:22.420Z`, source revision `e964a095ede1c077b36b6476af5ee85b087f52f8`, and publication ID `aea1e08b74f6b7835473ffb482baeddd42c97346d0a08868a66574f1a5d089ce`. Internal evidence changes have no deployable web-byte delta and create no new site release.
    TinyRustLM.MiRust.com: Active documentation-first TinyRustLM architecture, developer, and evidence portal. Remote `master` is policy commit `5ebbf32f31b54a3cc9637008d7020b46f832064c`; the protected local checkout remains at `c9cd240221c6ff6efd7ab5fcc476dad96f75ad01`. Local/live identity remains observed as `1.6.0`, updated `2026-07-12T22:00:00Z`; PHP is unavailable locally and no new deployment or immutable publication is claimed.
  publication_discipline:
    - Commit and push every coherent major change as soon as its affected build and checks are healthy. Do not hold a valid checkpoint for unrelated future perfection.
    - Publish every affected site promptly when its complete affected release gate passes. Internal-only changes with no deployable site-byte delta do not create a release. A failing build, test, documentation, security, authorization, transport, or readback gate remains an explicit blocker and never becomes a skip.
    - Before each site publish, assign an intentional semantic version and release date, update a human-readable update log plus an immutable machine-readable release ledger, bind the exact clean source revision and artifact hashes, run relevant tests and secret scans, and obtain publication authorization.
    - Commit and push every affected source, documentation, marketing, and release-log repository before claiming publication. Deploy only from its source-control truth, then verify public HTTPS readback, version, release date, update log, asset hashes, and behavior.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, MiniModel.MiRust.com, MiRust.com, and any retained redirect surfaces behaviorally and editorially consistent. Record an explicit blocker when a site cannot be updated; never call local files, package creation, upload attempts, or stale pages deployed.
    - Bring every retained active site onto one consistent immutable release-ledger contract; TinyRustLM.com is currently the only site in this inventory with `uaix.site_release.v1` publication evidence.
version_authority:
  current_version: 0.2.1
  next_version: 0.2.2
  policy: Increment intentionally after real implementation milestones; source scaffolding does not imply runtime support.
active_product:
  name: TinyRustLM
  root: tinyrustlm/
  purpose: Zero-dependency Rust/WASM browser-local SLM runtime and UI.
  enterprise_vnext_development_goal_2026_08_01: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-vnext-development-goal-memory-2026-08-01.md`, SHA256 `22838f84d8df1b7daef4577fa5f52fdbcf31e7f20eeeb377bf2b6f092c5b5731`, routes the 25-report enterprise vNext synthesis and active 60,899-byte execution assignment, SHA256 `629d7bee195f80c4acb868ed90c4124fd80d2cf6a1060a8fe13fdaa65968b31a`. It requires clean incompatible contracts, ten ADR gates, scalar-first conformance, bounded browser/runtime/security/release work, champion-plus-sealed-specialists, immutable evidence, and synchronized sites. The reports are advisory and every 20/50/25/40/20 campaign counter remains unearned until objective receipts exist.
  pre_release_no_debt_authority_2026_07_15: TinyRustLM is not a live released product. Until the human explicitly removes this rule, add no technical debt, legacy support, backward-compatibility paths, dual contracts, migration shims, deprecated aliases, or knowingly temporary architecture. Clean replacement, deletion of superseded implementation after verification, and full rewrites are authorized. Immutable receipts and dated failure evidence remain historical truth, not supported product behavior. This authority supersedes incompatible present-tense wording in older dated workspace entries.
  model_acquisition_v2_authority_2026_08_08: The current acquisition contract supersedes older conversion-kit and import-kit workflow entries. One user action selects a model. A complete identity-matched MiniModel P2P offer with its composition graph is preferred and is imported through the paired local companion; otherwise, after explicit companion pairing, protocol v2 performs immutable reviewed Hugging Face source download, bounded resumable hashing, Rust conversion, Rust receipt reinspection, `.slm` validation, base-only `.acg1` creation, composition reinspection, direct loopback streaming, and browser activation. Progress and typed failures stay in the app. Model acquisition and P2P sharing must not download README/TXT, shell, PowerShell, request JSON, conversion-kit, share-kit, or serving-helper files and must not require users to run scripts. TinyRustLM.com, MiniModel.org, UAIX.org, and MemoryEndpoints.com receive no prompts, responses, source tensors, model bytes, or composition bytes. Browser-only local `.slm` import remains valid; companion access is explicit, scoped, session-bound, and never probed before consent. The packaged companion and Rust converter are version 0.2.0 for this contract; release and public-deployment claims remain pending objective gates.
  third_party_review_storage_authority_2026_07_21: Keep all downloaded third-party repositories, packages, papers, standards, source archives, and model-review inputs outside project repositories and Git under `E:\Source\external\{project-name}`. Source control may contain original TinyRustLM work plus public-safe URLs, immutable revisions, byte counts, hashes, licenses, and bounded findings, but not copied third-party review trees or machine-local external paths.
  source_control_model_payload_boundary_2026_07_26: Current source control contains no candidate, trained, converted, product, source-checkpoint, raw-tensor, or P2P-piece model payloads. Only six explicitly allowlisted deterministic `.slm` fixtures of at most 64 KiB remain, and they are runtime/test evidence only. Browser boot has no built-in model and requires admitted local, selector-registry, companion, or P2P intake. A preservation-only external manifest with SHA256 `96795962727efcae9ee142ba31a4de7b8d891e176ef6373a6a518383e2155bca` reverified 6 `.slm` artifacts plus 8 source checkpoints, 16,259,130,576 total bytes, and zero partial files; it grants no quality, release, catalog, or campaign-counter authority. Older entries naming tracked model paths or bootstrap selectors are immutable history, not current product behavior.
  exact_flat_named_target_performance_2026_07_22: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-named-target-performance-memory-2026-07-22.md`, SHA256 `20620ef887db16098a3d7de942c101653fba77aee06cb1951f9c3a4e23e71a68`, routes preregistration SHA256 `269459766b1bab57ce86cadda296d0941d3dfc3d6876873ab48657ba7bd64c63`, preserved pre-execution failure `exact-flat-physical-target-attempt-1291be20cc291bc6`, observation `exact-flat-physical-target-20bfb3e18230f257`, and child receipt `exact-flat-physical-target-verification-6b478318ef8747cb` file SHA256 `4cf29cef23b057677e97ed0e03751bac6ad88d31fe44dff2d93582c22d437c1e`. Three preregistered workloads and 324 retained query samples verify latency, throughput, and process memory only on the named Windows host. Energy, independent chassis attestation, complete physical-target status, sealed-corpus quality, crash-recovered deletion, compression, product, training, and release remain false. Never rerun either physical-target `--write` command.
  exact_flat_browser_wasm_verification_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `b9191b867784c8c0323c8f2b484aca5c13c95a5766686a3da061cb35d83150a7`, routes v2 preregistration, committed runner, immutable observation `exact-flat-browser-wasm-0361d72f245abbd3` file SHA256 `d28c921ec1df7db538417aaed8803fce88bc6d37b3cbc5fcf5d291b0a91a6f9a`, and child receipt `exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-8fcdeb0b93534ca4` file SHA256 `5c52a2287390f79e6a4971da6a6455a69c4ebd52ac6473bcce5408fd62560157`. The exact three-module, 49-test set ran in two real Chromium processes; all entry points returned zero, processes closed, unique profiles were deleted, and page-network/error counters were zero. This grants only exact experiment real-browser execution; use the newer named-target route for bounded host measurements. Sealed-corpus quality, durable deletion, compression, TurboVec parity, product, training, and release remain unproved. Never rerun either browser `--write` command.
  colibri_public_source_pin_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-colibri-public-source-pin-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `3b3b36e1eb9daa8d4bb12787e20fed23e34559b2bfff58a640d0d9b213ac78fd`, routes direct review of public Colibri commit `44e489b196c9b7876b3d37a0570ebf1c6f90f54c`, tree `faae3d9594319ab856a4c3dd3f69a3afdd71f348`, and Apache-2.0 license. Default placement retains the full trained expert set on disk while changing residency; optional `CACHE_ROUTE=1` may change expert choice and needs its own quality gate. No upstream source entered TinyRustLM, and no compatibility, dependency, model-byte reduction, performance, quality, or adoption claim is authorized.
  exact_flat_retrieval_foundation_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-retrieval-foundation-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `6a0f3241253b1d666959984869c4ec29eb04c97fb67a446ccdb89bc26423de76`, routes the preregistered dependency-free exact f32 baseline. Preregistration SHA256 is `0d9b6b3d31a25cba843034ceeafca3a88bc1287546f66025b62d13ba14441152`; ledger SHA256 is `7daa7653222914a028e636e6de6e195f94cb5eb50d5bd10a76af624877303808`; receipt `exact-flat-retrieval-75f95baa316315ea` SHA256 is `893e96f461f701f46a3aaaeecddd67bc2b700625ccdb9f0d83ce4b0b67d8c18c`. Checked scalar search, persistence, corruption detection, deletion/compaction, native tests, and WASM compilation pass; separate browser and named-target children close exact module execution and bounded host measurements. Coverage, Miri, representative-corpus quality, and crash-recovered on-disk deletion remain open; no TurboVec parity, compression, product, training, or release authority exists.
  current_local_import_and_p2p_authority_2026_07_15: Local picker input is bounded to 1 GiB, read in 4 MiB slices into one exact final WASM allocation, and finalized through Rust-owned incremental SHA-256 and TinyRustLM checksum state before runtime adoption. Conversion and local share kits may create peer pieces, a peer-free base catalog, and consenting local companion/contact handoffs, but they cannot create public availability. Public announcement requires MiniModel `prepare-seed-announcement` with an external probe receipt, observer trust configuration, and seed fleet configuration. The only current deep conversion modes are `hf-conversion-kit-safetensors-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-review-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec`, and `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec`; the former aggregate mode is deleted. Loopback and mapped-host tests remain local evidence and never count as outside-network proof or a live-release claim.
  source_folder_correction_2026_07_08: E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com is the canonical TinyRustLM source folder. E:\Source\Rust\SLMComposer.com was the retired historical name and must not be used for active source work. On 2026-07-08 the full non-git, non-target, non-x64, non-user-file source tree from SLMComposer.com was mirrored into TinyRustLM.com; the Markdown research/intake files already placed under TinyRustLM.com\agent-file-handoff were preserved and restored. A post-migration source-content check excluding generated bin/obj output found zero missing non-build files in TinyRustLM.com; remaining content differences are intentional TinyRustLM.com-side memory/verifier corrections. E:\Source\Rust\SLMComposer.com was then deleted locally on 2026-07-08 and must not be recreated as a TinyRustLM source workspace.
  memory_endpoints_coordination_current: TinyRustLM optional hosted memory has public-safe routing hints for MemoryEndpoints expansion project `project-7474be75df6643b89953`, goal `goal-tinyrustlm-hosted-memory`, agent `tinyrustlm-agent`, and display name `TinyRustLM Agent`. Read `.uai/memory-endpoints-coordination.uai` and rediscover every authenticated room, project, company, workspace, task, route, and capability before use; cached IDs are hints, not current authority. This Codex session is not connected to or communicating with MemoryEndpoints.com, no individual user account has been inspected or validated, the production single-use enrollment contract is not advertised, and the live continuity campaign remains 0/25. Local `.uai` and Markdown are the current offline authority; credentials and protected authentication instructions stay outside repository memory.
  memory_endpoints_individual_agent_integration_prompt_2026_07_15: `agent-file-handoff/Improvement/2026-07-15-memoryendpoints-tinyrustlm-individual-agent-continuity-integration-prompt.md`, SHA256 `14eb7898df9a307169f14fa0bcada93cfc824f16d343c99b19649a1d70f29863`, is the standalone authorized-platform-agent assignment for creating atomic single-use enrollment, scoped agent tokens, hidden-workspace reconnect, 12-record virtual-UAIX continuity, explicit revision conflict handling, browser secret boundaries, 25 disposable-company live verification, cleanup, and content-addressed receipts. The prompt itself is not evidence of a live connection or a completed account configuration.
  memory_endpoints_prior_browser_evidence_2026_07_10: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-memory-endpoints-production-deployment-memory-2026-07-10.md` (SHA256 `50d1f973ce180c6aa0743fabe77696b75d1194bae15838accdaf3df8e9eae6f1`) and messages `meetmsg-01783708293173686051-c7455893` / `meetmsg-01783708293599563088-a79930af` are retained historical browser and hosted-status evidence only. They do not prove current production availability, the new single-use individual-agent enrollment contract, any present connection from this session, any user-account configuration, or one of the required 25 live continuity rounds.
  memory_endpoints_offline_sync_current: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-offline-memory-sync-implementation-2026-07-10.md` (SHA256 `56f5d5de7b7eff4d722c6b4e4870a29b5ba9089d1cba02b57bf2ebb44fd95df3`) before changing offline outbox, multi-tab coordination, reconnect ordering, retrieval packing, revisions, tombstones, device authority, checkpoints, compaction, or optional MemoryEndpoints NuGet APIs. F1/F2 pass six real-browser modes and visual lock; F3-F5 deterministic Rust/C#/browser contracts pass local proof but are not hosted-complete until MemoryEndpoints publishes authoritative receipt, revision/head/conflict, monotonic pull, index-watermark, tombstone-retention, and device-authority routes. Contract request messages are `meetmsg-01783719601736718792-a250a13b` in the goal room and `meetmsg-01783719608338263899-006c383c` in the expansion project room.
  memory_endpoints_prior_completion_audit_2026_07_10: `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-memory-endpoints-completion-audit.json`, SHA256 `d4e3015674db212efe93563d627b7fef8288e855fb90f0f5f4c7602618058b6e`, is retained evidence for its earlier bounded objective and secret-free report shape; it is not a current product-completion or live-campaign receipt.
  memory_endpoints_prior_hosted_distribution_receipt_2026_07_10: Status event `mem-26586666c00e4d84b090`, handoff event `mem-1079ad608ebd4947acb0`, and `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-memory-endpoints-production-hosted-distribution.json` (SHA256 `e4d25dbe2ac8a2e5e4136676f743a110169825e7fa86baee95a9c5f476dc297f`) remain historical hosted-distribution evidence. They do not satisfy the current single-use enrollment, per-agent reconnect, disposable-company cleanup, or 25-round live acceptance gate.
  tinyrustlm_quality_ui_lock_goal_2026_07_07: `docs/report-intake/2026-07-07/tinyrustlm-quality-ui-lock-goal-2026-07-07.md` preserves the active objective: keep the approved TinyRustLM.com UI/UX unchanged, add visual screenshot/signature locks, and make real `.slm` responses coherent through the Rust/WASM runtime without canned answers, browser fakes, hidden remote inference, weakened tests, or fixture/demo quality claims. Current implementation has no-cheat diagnostics/eval gates, six fixed plus six seeded-holdout honest eval cases with JSON object/key validation, manifest-backed model capability metadata (`tokenizer`, `tokenizer_checksum`, `context_length`, `output_contract`, `prompt_format`, `instruction_support`, `chat_support`, `quality_eval_status`, `intended_use`), eval/browser prompt-format routing, normalized sidecar evidence (`none`, `not-applicable`, `empty-output`), a quality-evidence path that does not require exact canned output, runtime quality filtering for degenerate repeated fixture output, live UI-lock evidence, and rebuilt WASM validation evidence. The provenance gate now rejects assistant-quality sidecars unless they declare `honest-assistant-quality-v1`, no-cheat pass, zero no-cheat failures, fixed plus holdout counts, a numeric holdout seed, per-case origin, and non-fixture/non-plumbing quality scope; converted-trained browser fixture bundles intentionally fail closed before selector admission when their eval evidence is `fixture-exact-v1`. Runtime `.slm` load validation now fails closed on malformed-but-checksummed tensor metadata, non-finite f32 payloads, and non-positive/non-finite q8/q4 scales; current served WASM manifest checksum is `0xfd09af080dd804f0`, ABI smoke proves `malformedSlmPayload=passed`, and browser `model-malformed` smoke proves the locked UI rejects a corrupt-but-checksummed q8 `.slm` as `Model rejected` / `error 6` / `invalid header` while keeping selector recovery available. `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -RunVisualLock` now verifies the approved desktop/mobile shell against the live baseline with screenshot evidence and `baseline_failures=[]`; Bash mirrors it with `RUN_VISUAL_LOCK=1`. The served SmolLM2-360M q4 route below is the first quality-capable `.slm` evidence on the same live UI/runtime path, and `assistant-prompt-cards` now proves visible Summarize/Code/Rewrite/JSON cards through that q4 path; product completion remains open for broader unseen-prompt polish, performance, deployment/live proof, and continued no-private-internals boundaries.
  smollm2_360m_q4_served_quality_2026_07_08: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/smollm2-gqa-gbpe-planning-memory-2026-07-08.md` now records the real served quality-capable model route: `tinyrustlm/models/smollm2-360m-instruct-q4.slm`, q4_0, `227667520` bytes, `.slm` checksum `0x8b5aa7ec4abeed93`, manifest checksum `0xa480d83d75c2d6ef`, runtime-smoke checksum `0x8d66c5368b03f5ce`, eval sidecar checksum `0x7f52ec0f8a1112b7`, eval case-evidence checksum `0xf63dee70df605f05`, tokenizer `gpt2-bpe-v1` checksum `0x8c86095c5c19f5cb`, ChatML prompt format, and shape vocab 49152 hidden 960 layers 32 heads 15 KV heads 5 ffn 2560 context 8192. Native validate/manifest/runtime-smoke/release eval/quality-gate all passed, release eval passed 12/12 fixed plus seeded holdout cases, `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -RunBrowserSmoke -BrowserSmokeModes assistant-quality` passed with selected model `smollm2q4`, response `Hello! Welcome to my browser-local AI assistant.`, q4 diagnostics, and eval/runtime sidecars fetched before model bytes, and `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -RunBrowserSmoke -BrowserSmokeModes assistant-prompt-cards` passed through visible starter cards with code `This code adds two integers together.` and JSON `{"status":"local","reason":"In browser local runtime model where prompts stay"}`. The same report now records runtime parser/loader fail-closed hardening, rebuilt WASM ABI proof for malformed-but-checksummed q8 scale rejection (`malformedSlmPayload=passed`, `invalid header`, WASM checksum `0xfd09af080dd804f0`), and browser `model-malformed` smoke proof with selected `tinylm16q8`, `/models/tinylm16-q8.slm`, `Model rejected`, `error 6`, `invalid header`, diagnostics `model_loaded=false`, disabled generate/reset/step controls, enabled selector, and no remote-origin requests. `smollm2q4` is first in the app model map and HTML bootstrap select.
  bleeding_edge_intake_processed_2026_07_08: `docs/report-intake/2026-07-08/MANIFEST.md`, `docs/report-intake/2026-07-08/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-intake-synthesis-2026-07-08.md`, `docs/report-intake/2026-07-08/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-tdd-plan-2026-07-08.md`, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-system-plan-memory-2026-07-08.md` process the 31-report Improvement batch into durable long-term memory and hot `.uai` routing. Use this route before changing runtime response quality, honest eval/no-cheat gates, `.slm` trust metadata, browser/WASM worker/cache behavior, MiniModel/P2P distribution, quantization/compression/distillation, model-candidate catalogs, or protected NuGet/open-core boundaries.
  stories15m_bpe_intake_2026_07_08: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/stories15m-bpe-safetensors-plan-memory-2026-07-08.md` records the first real Stories-15M compatible source-shape and conversion route: `stories15m-bpe` plans 56 tied-output raw f32 tensors for vocab 32000, hidden 288, 6 layers, 6 attention/KV heads, context 256, tokenizer strategy `llama-bpe-v1`, and `requires_tokenizer_artifact=true`. Browser Hugging Face requests default `Xenova/llama2.c-stories15M` and `ModelCloud/tinyllama-15M-stories` to `stories15m-bpe`; `source-template stories15m-bpe` intentionally fails closed until a reviewed tokenizer artifact is supplied. The actual downloaded `Xenova/llama2.c-stories15M` checkpoint plans, reviews, converts, and validates from `target/stories15m-hf-source/model.safetensors` with 56 tensors, 15,191,712 parameters, raw bytes `60766848`, tied `lm_head.weight` accepted as the embedding tensor only for tied-output shapes, reviewed tokenizer import `31741` learned rows and `61249` merges, and q8 `.slm` checksum `0x68ff664ad56b7193`. Runtime honest eval on the produced `stories15m-q8.slm` executes real local generations but fails assistant quality `0/12` because the checkpoint is a raw Stories completion model, not an instruction/chat assistant. This is real-model conversion progress only, not an assistant-quality claim.
