  protected_nuget_sdk: `dotnet/`, `rust/crates/`, `eng/`, `.github/workflows/`, and `docs/nuget/` now carry the protected TinyRustLM NuGet distribution: `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, `TinyRustLM.P2P`, and `TinyRustLM.Memory` expose `.slm` validation/inspection, native-backed runtime harness operations, metadata-bound P2P share/import workflows, local manifest-piece verification, `.slm` assembly, receipt sidecars, receipt-sidecar inspection, and UAIX `.uai` memory/persona package planning and inspection through the `tinyrustlm-native` C ABI while deliberately excluding `slm_pack`, private conversion internals, quantization authoring, adapter authoring/auto-assembly, selector generation, offline breeding, lineage promotion, eval/provenance authoring, premium routing/optimizer logic, encryption-key handling, telemetry, license-server internals, commercial orchestration, hosted memory import validation, persona-fidelity certification, automatic repo writes, and private training/model-ranking/memory-optimization logic. The package/audit/publish/feed scripts validate the four protected `TinyRustLM.*` packages for public release. The local UAIX Browser folder feed can also emit `UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions`, `UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime`, `UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P`, `UAIX.Browser.Memory`, and the controlled local `UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion` wrapper under `E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET` with old root packages archived first.
  nuget_pack_sha256_manifest_2026_07_06: `eng\pack.ps1` and `eng/pack.sh` write `SHA256SUMS-<PackageIdPrefix>-<version>.txt` after packing from the source-declared version and exact package ID set, replace same-prefix stale manifests, and fail closed if an expected current `.nupkg` is missing; the Browser feed audit consumes `SHA256SUMS-UAIX.Browser-<version>.txt`.
  nuget_publish_sha256_manifest_binding_2026_07_06: `eng\publish-nuget.ps1` and `eng/publish-nuget.sh` now require `SHA256SUMS-TinyRustLM-<version>.txt` to exist beside the four protected public packages and match the exact push set before dry-run, missing-key, ready-to-push, pushed, or push-failed evidence can be written; `eng\verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1` and `.sh` reject publish plans that are not bound to a passing SHA256SUMS manifest, and publish-plan/feed-hash reports carry the SHA256SUMS manifest path/hash/match evidence.
  nuget_public_doc_site_audit_2026_07_06: `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1` and `eng/verify-public-doc-sites.sh` write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-public-doc-sites-audit.json` with schema `tinyrustlm.docs.public_site_audit.v0`, proving sibling TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and MiniModel.MiRust.com docs mention the four protected packages including `TinyRustLM.Memory`, include SHA256SUMS-bound publish/feed-hash wording, and contain no stale three-package release-status claims.
