  uaix_browser_nuget_org_published_0_1_6_2026_07_07: `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, and `dotnet/Directory.Build.props` were advanced to source/package version `0.1.6` so the native UAIX memory deployment-report inspection fix could ship in an immutable NuGet version. `eng\pack.ps1 -PackageOutput E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET -PackageIdPrefix UAIX.Browser -AbstractionsPackageId UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions -CorePackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime -P2PPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P -MemoryPackageId UAIX.Browser.Memory -ConversionPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion -IncludePrivateConversion -ArchiveOtherPackages` rebuilt native, ran `TinyRustLM.Core.Tests` 40/40 and `TinyRustLM.Package.Tests` 41/41, archived old same-prefix root package files, and wrote five `0.1.6` `.nupkg` files, five matching `.snupkg` sidecars, `README-UAIX.Browser-0.1.6.txt`, and `SHA256SUMS-UAIX.Browser-0.1.6.txt` to `E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET`. Local `eng\verify-browser-feed.ps1` and clean consumer smoke passed at `0.1.6` with `memory files 62` and `conversion validated`; readiness with the local NuGet API-key file reported `ready_to_publish`; `eng\publish-browser-nuget.ps1` authenticated-pushed all five packages plus all five symbols to NuGet.org with `artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json` recording `status=pushed`, `package_version=0.1.6`, `package_count=5`, `symbol_package_count=5`, and `secret_material_included=false`. After indexing, NuGet.org `eng\verify-feed-current.ps1` passed with all five package IDs exposing `0.1.6` as current, `eng\verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1` passed against the publish plan while accepting NuGet.org repository signatures, `eng\verify-consumer.ps1` was strengthened to build and inspect a full 62-file Advanced Persona Profile package containing `reports/deployment-memory-and-test-report.uai`, and both local-folder and NuGet.org `0.1.6` consumer smokes passed with that full package inspection plus `memory files 62` and `conversion validated`. `eng\audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.ps1` wrote `artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness.json` with `status=published_current`, `package_id_count=5`, `publish_plan_package_count=5`, `publish_plan_symbol_package_count=5`, and `secret_material_included=false`. Public TinyRustLM/MiniModel documentation status surfaces and `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1` / `.sh` were updated to require the branded Browser lane at `0.1.6`.
  uaix_browser_nuget_org_published_0_1_7_2026_07_07: `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `dotnet/Directory.Build.props`, public status docs, and public-doc verifiers were advanced to source/package version `0.1.7` so the Browser lane includes the latest package docs/status and safe release-readiness dry-run plan boundary. `eng\pack.ps1 -PackageOutput E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET -PackageIdPrefix UAIX.Browser -AbstractionsPackageId UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions -CorePackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime -P2PPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P -MemoryPackageId UAIX.Browser.Memory -ConversionPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion -IncludePrivateConversion -ArchiveOtherPackages` rebuilt native, ran `TinyRustLM.Core.Tests` 40/40 and `TinyRustLM.Package.Tests` 41/41, archived old same-prefix `0.1.6` root feed files under `E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET\Archive`, and wrote five `0.1.7` `.nupkg` files, five matching `.snupkg` sidecars, `README-UAIX.Browser-0.1.7.txt`, and `SHA256SUMS-UAIX.Browser-0.1.7.txt`. Local `eng\verify-browser-feed.ps1 -PackageSource E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET -PackageVersion 0.1.7` passed, local clean consumer smoke passed with `memory files 62` and `conversion validated`, and readiness with the local NuGet API-key file reported `ready_to_publish` before push. `eng\publish-browser-nuget.ps1 -PackageVersion 0.1.7` authenticated-pushed all five packages plus all five symbols to NuGet.org with `artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json` recording `status=pushed`, `package_version=0.1.7`, `package_count=5`, `symbol_package_count=5`, and `secret_material_included=false`. Post-indexing `eng\verify-feed-current.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PackageVersion 0.1.7 -PackageIds UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions,UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime,UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P,UAIX.Browser.Memory,UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-org-feed-current-20260707-0.1.7.json` passed with all five package IDs exposing `0.1.7` as current, `eng\verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PublishPlanReport artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-org-feed-hashes-20260707-0.1.7.json` passed with zero package-integrity mismatches while accepting five NuGet.org repository signatures, `eng\audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.ps1 -PackageVersion 0.1.7 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-20260707-0.1.7.json` reported `published_current`, and `eng\verify-consumer.ps1 -PackageSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PackageVersion 0.1.7 -CorePackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime -P2PPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P -MemoryPackageId UAIX.Browser.Memory -ConversionPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion` passed with `memory files 62` and `conversion validated`. A fresh-publish consumer smoke initially exposed stale .NET NuGet HTTP metadata cache behavior; `eng\verify-consumer.ps1` and `.sh` now isolate `NUGET_HTTP_CACHE_PATH` alongside `NUGET_PACKAGES`, with targeted and full `TinyRustLM.Package.Tests` 41/41 passing. Public doc audits passed with `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-public-doc-sites-browser-nuget-0.1.7-audit.json` and Bash `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-public-doc-sites-browser-nuget-0.1.7-audit-bash.json`.
  uaix_browser_nuget_readiness_safe_plan_refresh_2026_07_07: Live NuGet.org and local folder-feed evidence was refreshed for the five `UAIX.Browser.*` package IDs at immutable version `0.1.6`: `eng\verify-feed-current.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PackageVersion 0.1.6 -PackageIds UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions,UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime,UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P,UAIX.Browser.Memory,UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-org-feed-current-20260707-refresh.json` passed; `eng\verify-browser-feed.ps1 -PackageSource E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET -PackageVersion 0.1.6 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-feed-audit-20260707-refresh.json` passed; `eng\verify-consumer.ps1 -PackageSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PackageVersion 0.1.6 -CorePackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime -P2PPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P -MemoryPackageId UAIX.Browser.Memory -ConversionPackageId UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion` passed with `memory files 62` and `conversion validated`; and `eng\verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PublishPlanReport artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-org-feed-hashes-20260707-refresh.json` passed. A pre-fix readiness run exposed that `eng\audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.ps1` / `.sh` defaulted their dry-run publish plan to the canonical `uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json`, which could clobber retained post-push evidence during routine freshness checks; both scripts now default to `artifacts/reports/uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-publish-plan-dry-run.json` unless `-PublishPlanReport` / `UAIX_BROWSER_PUBLISH_PLAN_REPORT` explicitly selects another readiness path. `README.md`, `docs/nuget/README.md`, `docs/nuget/PRIVATE_FEED.md`, and `docs/nuget/PACKAGE_SECURITY.md` document that separation. Verified commands: PowerShell parse for `eng\audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.ps1`, `bash -n eng/audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.sh`, targeted `BrowserReleaseReadinessScriptsWriteMachineReadableReport`, full `dotnet test dotnet\tests\TinyRustLM.Package.Tests\TinyRustLM.Package.Tests.csproj` 41/41, `eng\audit-browser-nuget-release-readiness.ps1 -PackageSource E:\Source\WP\UAIX-Publish\DOTNET-NUGET -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -PackageVersion 0.1.6 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-20260707-safe-plan-refresh.json` with `status=published_current`, Bash parity with `/mnt/e/Source/WP/UAIX-Publish/DOTNET-NUGET` writing `artifacts/reports\uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-20260707-safe-plan-refresh-bash.json` with `status=published_current`, and `git diff --check` with CRLF warnings only. These source docs/tooling changes were shipped in the immutable `0.1.7` Browser package lane.
  public_docs_browser_readiness_safe_plan_refresh_2026_07_07: TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and MiniModel.MiRust.com public docs/LLMS surfaces now mention the dedicated readiness dry-run plan path `uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-publish-plan-dry-run.json` so routine release-readiness audits do not overwrite the retained pushed-package evidence in `uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json`. `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1` and `.sh` now require that term in the Browser publish public-doc gate. Verified commands: PowerShell parse for `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1`, `bash -n eng/verify-public-doc-sites.sh`, `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-public-doc-sites-browser-readiness-safe-plan-audit.json`, `bash eng/verify-public-doc-sites.sh artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-public-doc-sites-browser-readiness-safe-plan-audit-bash.json`, targeted `BrowserReleaseReadinessScriptsWriteMachineReadableReport`, and main/TinyRustLM.com/TinyRustLM.MiRust.com/MiniModel.org/MiniModel.MiRust.com `git diff --check` with CRLF warnings only. These public-doc and verifier updates are post-0.1.6 source state; any future package-content publication must use a new immutable version.
  local_connect_endpoint_unknown_app_category_binding_2026_07_07: TinyRustLM Local Connect browser approval state now persists endpoint-derived app category overrides for approved app names that are not in the built-in known-app map, prunes stale overrides when the approved-app list changes, exports canonical `approved_app_bindings` with the row-selected category, and rejects app-level approval when a known app name is reported under a conflicting endpoint category. The mock endpoint smoke now lists `AcmeDocs.exe` as an unknown `documents` app and requires the exported binding to remain `documents`; the real Rust endpoint smoke keeps verifying the same binding contract through its built-in `winword.exe` row. Documentation in `tinyrustlm/README.md`, `tinyrustlm/docs/browser-runtime.md`, and `tinyrustlm/docs/testing.md` records the boundary. Verified commands: `node --check tinyrustlm\app\app.js`, `node --check tinyrustlm\tools\browser-smoke.js`, `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-local-connect`, `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -BrowserSmokeModes local-connect-endpoint-ui,local-connect-rust-endpoint-ui -BrowserSmokeTimeoutSeconds 300 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-ui-local-connect-approval-binding-verification.json`, `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -BrowserSmokeModes local-connect-approval-ui -BrowserSmokeTimeoutSeconds 300 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-ui-local-connect-approval-drawer-verification.json`, and `git diff --check` with CRLF warnings only.
