  tinyrustlm_split_deep_review_reject_branch_verified_2026_07_07: Targeted branch command `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -Port 8192 -DebugPort 9522 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-ui-hf-review-reject-verification.json -BrowserSmokeModes hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec -BrowserSmokeTimeoutSeconds 900` passed. The report has `browser_smoke_mode=hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec`, `deep_browser_smoke_requested=true`, `browser_smoke_timeout_seconds=900`, and a per-mode report at `artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec-smoke.json`; `UiVerificationReportIsMachineReadableWhenPresent` passed against that report. The smoke evidence includes `reviewConversionKitFailure`, request inspection output, a conversion preflight report, and Rust rejection before conversion with a Hugging Face source byte-count mismatch, leaving no successful conversion branch field for the narrow mode. A strict post-run process check found no verifier-owned `node`, `cargo`, `tinyrustlm-local-server`, `tinyrustlm-slm-pack`, or `tinyrustlm-browser-smoke` process for ports 8192/9522 or the review-reject mode. Full split deep execution across safetensors success, review success, GGUF success, and P2P import remains a manual CI/release-candidate gate unless each targeted mode is run.
  tinyrustlm_full_split_deep_gate_verified_2026_07_07: The remaining split deep browser smokes passed both individually and as the combined CI-style release-candidate command. Individual commands passed for `hf-conversion-kit-safetensors-exec` on port/debug 8193/9532, `hf-conversion-kit-review-exec` on 8194/9542, `hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec` on 8195/9552, and `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` on 8196/9562, each writing a `tinyrustlm-ui-hf-*-verification.json` wrapper report. The exact combined command `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -Port 8197 -DebugPort 9572 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-ui-deep-verification.json -BrowserSmokeModes hf-conversion-kit-safetensors-exec,hf-conversion-kit-review-exec,hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec,hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec,hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` passed, and `UiVerificationReportIsMachineReadableWhenPresent` passed against `artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-ui-deep-verification.json`. The combined report records all five deep modes as `pass` and points to the per-mode smoke files. Content spot checks found `conversionKitExecution`, `reviewConversionKitExecution`, `reviewConversionKitFailure`, `ggufConversionKitExecution`, and `p2pImportKitExecution`; the P2P smoke includes peer-import request validation, offline request inspection, receiver-validation contract validation, import receipt validation, peer import receipt-chain validation, and import receipt ledger validation. A strict post-run process check for deep ports/debug ports, browser-smoke, and local-server patterns found no verifier-owned processes. Final verification also passed full `TinyRustLM.Package.Tests` 40/40, `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1`, and `git diff --check` with CRLF warnings only.
  tinyrustlm_public_root_loopback_gate_refreshed_2026_07_07: `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-public-root.ps1 -Root E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com -Port 8241 -DebugPort 9741 -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-public-root-verification.json` passed against mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:8241/` with `public_host_mapping=tinyrustlm.com-loopback-browser-smoke`. The `tinyrustlm.public_root_verification.v0` report records `status=pass`; `public-default-demo` proves the real first-run MiniModel demo autoload reaches `Ready` and generates, while non-demo public-root modes launch with `?autoload=0` to isolate local import, ambiguous import rejection, unsafe peer URL rejection, UAIX memory deck, Local Connect approval, Local Connect endpoint, Rust endpoint, and live peer-status metadata checks.
  tinyrustlm_ui_smoke_timeout_reporting_2026_07_07: `eng\verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1` has `-BrowserSmokeTimeoutSeconds` defaulting to 1800 seconds and runs browser smoke subprocesses through a timeout-aware launcher that writes the per-mode report file before failing and kills the spawned process tree on timeout. Non-browser child processes also drain stdout/stderr concurrently and have an owned-process timeout. `eng/verify-tinyrustlm-ui.sh` mirrors browser timeout reporting with `BROWSER_SMOKE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`. Rerun only the named targeted branch when deeper evidence is needed; no aggregate compatibility mode exists.
  public_doc_sites_nuget_status_refresh_2026_07_07: TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and MiniModel.MiRust.com checked docs were refreshed to distinguish the protected source-level `TinyRustLM.*` lane from the public `UAIX.Browser.*` NuGet.org lane published at `0.1.5`. `eng\verify-public-doc-sites.ps1` and `.sh` now require the five branded Browser package IDs, `0.1.5`, and post-publish verification wording on checked public docs, and reject stale `NuGet.org has zero listed versions`, `NuGet.org reports zero listed versions`, `blocked_missing_api_key`, and old package-version publication-status text. PowerShell doc-site audit passed after the refresh; PHP CLI was not installed locally for `php -l`, so the repaired PHP page registry was structurally checked by readback and public-doc audit instead.
  nuget_repository_signature_hash_verifier_2026_07_06: `eng\verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1` and `.sh` still require exact package SHA-256 and byte-count matches for local/private folder feeds. For NuGet v3 feeds, if exact bytes differ after publication, the verifier downloads the package, compares every original local package entry by path, byte count, and SHA-256, and accepts the feed only when the only additional entry is NuGet.org's `.signature.p7s` repository signature. Reports preserve `hash_mismatch_count`/`byte_count_mismatch_count` while passing only when `package_integrity_mismatch_count=0` and recording `repository_signature_accepted_count`.
  nuget_public_feed_check_2026_07_06: `eng\verify-feed-current.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-nuget-org-feed-current.json` wrote `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-org-feed-current.json` with `status=fail`, `package_version=0.1.1`, and zero listed versions for `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P`; `eng\publish-nuget.ps1 -SkipVerification -DryRun` then wrote `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-publish-plan.json` with `status=dry_run`, `package_count=3`, audit match true, SHA-256/byte-count evidence for the three local packages, `source_provenance_available=true`, git commit/branch/dirty-tree evidence, tracked/untracked change counts, and `secret_material_included=false`. `eng\audit-nuget-release-readiness.ps1` / `.sh` now write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-release-readiness.json`; the current environment reports `blocked_missing_api_key` after local publish-plan/feed-current/feed-hash gates pass and NuGet.org still lacks the declared version. Public NuGet.org availability is still incomplete until an authenticated publish plus post-publish feed-current/feed-hash verification passes.
  nuget_p2p_url_hardening_2026_07_06: `tinyrustlm-p2p` now validates `PublicBaseUrl` directly before writing a P2P announcement instead of appending a synthetic route; generated/received announcement URLs accept HTTPS or explicit-port loopback HTTP only and reject credentials, whitespace, query strings, fragments, backslashes, dot-segment traversal, and encoded dot/slash/backslash traversal. Rust tests cover accepted HTTPS/loopback bases and unsafe URL rejection, and package-boundary tests assert the public SDK crate no longer contains the old sentinel route.
  nuget_p2p_announcement_conflict_gate_2026_07_06: `tinyrustlm-p2p` now treats `peer_id + manifest_id` as a stable announcement identity: exact honest replays still deduplicate by `peer_id + manifest_id + manifest_sha256`, but received announcements and existing catalogs fail closed when the same peer/manifest identity changes model id, manifest URL, manifest SHA-256, artifact SHA-256, or artifact byte count. Rust and .NET tests cover the public SDK rejection path.
  nuget_p2p_catalog_inspection_gate_2026_07_06: The public SDK now exposes typed `P2PAnnouncementCatalogInspection` / `InspectAnnouncementCatalogJson` through Rust, C ABI, and .NET; it validates existing `tinyrustlm.p2p_announcement_catalog.v0` JSON, reports catalog SHA-256, announcement/peer/manifest/model counts, total announced artifact bytes, and valid status, and rejects catalog JSON above 4 MiB before parsing. Clean consumer scripts and package-boundary tests cover the API.
  nuget_p2p_signed_manifest_verification_2026_07_06: The protected NuGet P2P SDK now exposes local signed-manifest verification through Rust `verify_signed_manifest_text`, native `tinyrustlm_p2p_verify_signed_manifest_json`, and .NET `TinyRustLmP2PClient.VerifySignedManifest` / `VerifySignedManifestJson`. It verifies `tinyrustlm.p2p_signed_manifest.v0` envelopes against metadata-only `minimodel.public_key.v0` JSON, requiring the wrapped manifest to validate, `signature.kind=external-signature-v0`, canonical payload SHA-256 agreement, `ed25519-base64:` signature bytes, matching publisher/key/route/public-key SHA, `usage=minimodel-manifest-signing-v0`, and `revoked=false`; signing, key hosting, remote key discovery, transparency logs, and commercial publisher services remain outside the package.
  nuget_workspace_quality_gate_2026_07_06: `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`, and `eng\verify-package.ps1` now pass after runtime, `slm_pack`, and native ABI cleanup. The package verifier itself now runs `cargo fmt --all --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` before Rust tests, so CI/release cannot publish protected NuGet packages if workspace rustfmt or clippy regresses. The runtime crate now includes a real `tinyrustlm-eval` CLI wrapper around `eval_runner::run_eval_to_sidecar`, with integration coverage that invokes the binary and verifies the fixture eval sidecar. The full workspace test run includes local-connect approval policy tests, P2P signed-manifest tests, 82 runtime library tests plus eval CLI coverage, 455 `slm_pack` tests, GGUF conversion CLI tests, Hugging Face conversion CLI tests, and doc tests; the NuGet verifier rebuilt the native bridge, ran rustfmt/clippy plus Rust/.NET tests, packed `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P`, wrote `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-package-audit.json`, and passed clean consumer `.slm` runtime plus P2P share/import/receipt smoke from local package references.
  nuget_generation_options_gate_2026_07_06: The .NET runtime wrapper and Rust public runtime SDK now validate generation options before runtime mutation. .NET rejects non-positive `MaxNewTokens`, non-finite or negative `Temperature`, `TopK` outside 1..1024, and non-finite/out-of-range `TopP` as managed `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` values before P/Invoke; direct native callers now receive an `invalid_generation_options` JSON envelope for the same contract before runtime-handle lookup or lossy f64-to-f32 casts.
  nuget_managed_string_nul_gate_2026_07_06: The .NET wrapper now rejects embedded NUL characters before P/Invoke for paths, prompts, JSON handoff documents, optional catalog JSON, and P2P share-kit request fields, preventing native C-string truncation at the public SDK boundary.
  nuget_empty_string_native_bridge_2026_07_06: The .NET bridge now marshals empty strings as native empty C strings instead of null pointers, so empty prompts are preserved through runtime generation while null remains the sentinel for omitted optional native arguments.
  nuget_managed_share_kit_request_gate_2026_07_06: `TinyRustLmP2PClient` now validates `PrepareShareKitRequest` before serializing native JSON, rejecting missing `ModelPath` / `OutputDir` and `PieceSize` outside 1 KiB through 16 MiB as managed argument errors while leaving deeper URL, identifier, manifest, and artifact validation in the Rust P2P SDK.
  nuget_managed_p2p_json_budget_gate_2026_07_06: `TinyRustLmP2PClient` now mirrors Rust P2P JSON byte budgets before P/Invoke, rejecting manifests or signed-manifest envelopes over 1 MiB, public-key JSON over 16 KiB, announcements or local import receipts over 256 KiB, and announcement catalogs over 4 MiB as managed argument errors before native allocation or parsing.
  nuget_declared_package_file_audit_gate_2026_07_06: `eng/write-package-audit.ps1` and `.sh` now record declared package files from nuspec readme/license metadata, list package documentation entries, fail when declared README/license files are missing from `.nupkg` contents, and expose `missing_package_file_count` in the package-audit report.
  nuget_package_documentation_hash_parity_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now list expected package documentation entries with source/package SHA-256 values and fail when packaged README/license/package docs do not byte-match the current `docs/nuget` source files.
  nuget_exact_package_set_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now list the expected source-versioned package names plus missing/unexpected package entries and fail if `artifacts/packages` contains anything except `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P` at the source-declared version.
  nuget_package_identity_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record expected package ID/version for each protected `.nupkg` and fail if nuspec `id` or `version` differs from the protected filename and source-declared package version.
  nuget_public_dependency_graph_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record expected dependency entries plus missing/unexpected dependency entries and fail if protected packages drift away from the public graph: Abstractions has no package dependencies, Core depends only on same-version Abstractions, and P2P depends only on same-version Abstractions and Core.
  nuget_dependency_metadata_policy_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit expected dependency entries now include `exclude=Build,Analyzers`, and missing/unexpected dependency checks fail if protected package references drift from that dependency metadata policy.
  nuget_native_asset_placement_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record `unexpected_native_entries` plus `unexpected_native_entry_count` and fail if native runtime entries appear outside `TinyRustLM.Core`, keeping Abstractions and P2P as managed public API/metadata packages.
  nuget_native_asset_filename_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record `allowed_native_entries` and fail if `TinyRustLM.Core` carries native files outside the approved RID/native filename set: Windows `tinyrustlm_native.dll`, Linux `libtinyrustlm_native.so`, and macOS `libtinyrustlm_native.dylib`.
  nuget_package_entry_allowlist_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record `package_entry_names`, `allowed_package_entry_patterns`, and `unexpected_package_content_entries`, and fail if a protected `.nupkg` contains anything outside NuGet metadata, nuspec, README/license, package docs, `lib/net8.0` DLL/XML outputs, or approved Core native assets.
  nuget_public_api_surface_audit_gate_2026_07_06: package-audit reports now record `public_api_entries`, `expected_public_api_entries`, `missing_public_api_entries`, and `unexpected_public_api_entries` from packaged XML docs, and fail if Abstractions/Core/P2P/Memory expose public managed members outside the approved SDK contract.
  nuget_binary_public_surface_gate_2026_07_06: post-pack package tests now reflect packaged assemblies and fail if exported types, public constructor arity, DTO properties, or declared workflow methods drift outside the approved Abstractions/Core/P2P/Memory binary SDK contract.
  minimodel_manifest_signature_gate_2026_07_06: MiniModel signed manifests now fail closed unless `signature.kind=external-signature-v0`, comments are absent, `signature.key_id` is present, `signature.public_key_route` is safe, and `signature.payload_sha256` exactly matches the canonical sorted non-signature manifest body; `minimodel verify-manifest` prints that canonical digest for publisher review, and `minimodel verify-signed-manifest <manifest> <public-key-json>` performs local Ed25519 verification against metadata-only `minimodel.public_key.v0` JSON with matching publisher/key/route/SHA usage and `revoked=false`. Transparency-log inclusion and remote key-discovery policy remain future work.
  peer_source_announcement_overlay: TinyRustLM can apply a user-selected `minimodel.peer_source_announcement` JSON to an already loaded proof-ready `models.v0.json` catalog only when it carries the current version-1 complete-transfer envelope. The verifier requires proof version 1, complete-transfer status and scope, exact downloaded piece count, downloaded artifact byte count and SHA-256, dynamic checked-route count, bound model/artifact/peer identities, current expiry, no-project-server-byte flags, and an exact peer-offer match. Sampled proof version 0 is rejected with no compatibility path.
  catalog_announcement_feed_routes: TinyRustLM can follow `peer_source_announcement_route`, `peer_source_announcement_routes`, or `peer_source_announcement_feeds` from a loaded/default catalog only when each route stays on the catalog origin, the fetched metadata matches the declared SHA-256, the feed envelope is metadata-only, duplicate model/peer rows are absent, and every nonempty row passes the current version-1 complete-transfer announcement verifier plus exact peer-offer matching. Empty feeds remain valid checks that create no peer source; failed or stale feeds leave base metadata intact.
  catalog_announcement_route_budget_smoke: `hf-catalog-announcement-route-budget-ui` serves an oversized same-origin catalog-declared peer-source announcement route, proves TinyRustLM reports `Peer-source announcement metadata exceeded browser budget`, leaves the base proof-ready row at `Set Peer URL`, saves no peer import request/script, and fetches no MiniModel or Hugging Face model bytes.
  converted_once_publication_package: Hugging Face conversion scripts create local peer pieces, a peer-free base catalog, local receipts, and optional consenting peer-companion/contact/inventory handoffs after Rust accepts the artifact. They never generate an announcement, announcement feed, feed-bound catalog, or with-peer catalog. Public availability is a separate `prepare-seed-announcement` operation after current signed outside-network complete-transfer proof, observer trust, and fleet configuration exist.
  peer_contact_card_ui: TinyRustLM can load `minimodel.peer_contact_card` JSON from the simple P2P panel or Advanced source details, validate the metadata-only envelope, reviewed direct HTTP peer URL, no-project-server flags, and Rust-reverify-required boundary, then set the list-level Known peer URL and refresh proof-ready rows to `P2P Import` without fetching model bytes.
  peer_companion_inventory_ui: TinyRustLM can load `minimodel.peer_companion_inventory.v0` JSON from the simple P2P panel or Advanced source details, validate the metadata-only boundary, safe direct peer URL, companion-state and piece-store evidence, receipt-ledger/contact-card summaries, command hints, quota, serve-plan routes, and Rust-reverify-required fields, then show the peer URL/status route and fill plus persist the list-level Known peer URL for later P2P import request/script generation without fetching peer-piece or artifact bytes. `peer-companion-inventory-ui` proves drift rejection, Known peer input/local-storage handoff, and local-only network requests; `hf-peer-companion-inventory-ui` proves that same inventory-derived Known peer URL promotes a proof-ready Hugging Face row to `P2P Import` and is emitted into the downloaded `minimodel.peer_import_request.v0` plus `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` route/gate script from both source `/app/` and mapped TinyRustLM.com root assets.
  root_peer_contact_card_ui_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/ <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 hf-peer-contact-card-ui` is green against the packaged TinyRustLM.com root through loopback host mapping; it proves public-host card controls load, metadata-only `minimodel.peer_contact_card` input sets Known peer URL, proof-ready rows become `P2P Import`, and the generated peer import request/script use the card URL without project-hosted model bytes.
  root_peer_contact_card_reject_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/ <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 hf-peer-contact-card-reject-ui` is green against the packaged TinyRustLM.com root; it feeds an unsafe card that declares project-server model-byte serving and proves the UI fails closed with the unsafe flag in status, `Set Peer URL` retained, and no peer import request/script download.
  peer_url_unsafe_ui_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js <app-url> <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 peer-url-unsafe-ui` is green against source and mapped TinyRustLM.com root; it proves Known peer URL input rejects traversal paths, query/fragment URLs, non-plain host text, and project/Hugging Face root-dot or subdomain host variants before saving a peer URL, while accepting `http://127.0.0.1:8123/peer-pieces/`.
  converted_once_command_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/converted-once-p2p-smoke.js` proves deterministic Hugging Face-style local `.safetensors` fixture generation, Rust `convert-huggingface-request` `.slm` conversion with version-2 receipt, MiniModel `prepare-peer-share`, a peer-free catalog snapshot, local peer-companion/contact/inventory handoffs, and no-project-server-byte assertions. It requires zero generated peer sources and no announcement/feed output.
  huggingface_conversion_cli_smoke: `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-slm-pack --test huggingface_conversion_cli` proves the public packer binary can inspect browser-saved Hugging Face conversion requests before source-byte work, write deterministic Hugging Face-shaped single-file and sharded `.safetensors` fixtures, run `convert-huggingface-request` against a reviewed file or shard directory, validate the produced `.slm`, record preflight/receipt evidence including source file counts and contract status, fail closed on source SHA-256 drift with no `.slm` or conversion receipt, inspect GGUF request metadata while blocking GGUF requests from the safetensors converter, and reject unsafe Hugging Face model ids, unsafe `.safetensors`/`.gguf` file names, unsafe source input modes, or unsafe known peer URLs before source inspection or output-directory creation.
  huggingface_conversion_request_inspection: `inspect-huggingface-conversion-request <request.json> [output.report]` writes a source-byte-free request report with request SHA-256, source format, source input mode, supported/default source shape, default quantization, expected safetensors/GGUF file rows, no-project-server byte flags, and the required next gate. Browser-generated safetensors and GGUF conversion kits now run this before local source-byte inspection and write `tinyrustlm-conversion.request.inspect`.
  native_eval_cli_smoke: `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-runtime` now builds the documented `tinyrustlm-eval` binary and runs it against checked-in `.slm`, manifest, and eval-case fixtures, proving the native eval sidecar command path remains executable.
  browser_generated_conversion_kit_exec: The exact browser-generated conversion downloads are exercised by independent `hf-conversion-kit-safetensors-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-review-exec`, and `hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec` modes. All scripts write `tinyrustlm-conversion.request.inspect` before source-byte conversion, produce verified `.slm` and version-2 conversion receipt evidence, create MiniModel peer pieces plus a peer-free base catalog, and may create local companion/contact handoffs. They do not generate an announcement; the handoff records only the later proof-gated `prepare-seed-announcement` command shape.
  browser_generated_review_conversion_fail_closed: `hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec` runs the exact generated review script against an unreconciled source contract. Rust records `source_contract_status=fail` and `conversion_decision=source-contract-rejected-before-conversion`, exits nonzero before conversion, and leaves no `.slm`, receipt, or MiniModel peer-share output.
  huggingface_source_contract: Hugging Face conversion requests are source-contract-bound when metadata provides expected `.safetensors` file names, byte counts, and SHA-256 values; Rust `convert-huggingface-request` rejects unsafe model/source/known-peer identifiers before source reads, rejects mismatched local files or shard directories during preflight, writes `source_contract_status=fail`, produces no `.slm` or receipt, and records pass evidence in both preflight and receipt when local source bytes match.
  huggingface_sharded_source_directory: Rust `convert-huggingface-request` accepts either one reviewed local `.safetensors` file or a reviewed directory of `.safetensors` shards. Browser metadata records the full source contract, and `hf-conversion-kit-review-exec` verifies two SHA-256-bound shards, `source_file_count=2`, conversion, version-2 receipt inspection, peer-free catalog output, and local companion/contact handoffs without project-server model bytes.
  huggingface_gguf_review_conversion_kit: Hugging Face rows with safe `.gguf` siblings save a review-first GGUF conversion kit. `hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec` verifies request inspection, GGUF inspect/plan/dequantize/convert, `.slm` validation, MiniModel peer pieces, a peer-free base catalog, local companion/contact handoffs, and the external-proof-only announcement boundary.
  huggingface_availability_summary: The simple Hugging Face panel renders compact availability chips from the same row decision state that chooses `P2P Import`, `Set Peer URL`, `Start Conversion`, review, local `.slm`, no-source, and P2P-disabled actions; the chips clarify real availability without introducing desktop or network requirements into first-run search.
  simple_local_catalog_and_hf_prioritization: The simple P2P panel exposes `Local models.v0.json` / `Load Local Catalog`, so beginner users can load converted-once metadata snapshots without Advanced Tools; Hugging Face search fetches a wider metadata page and ranks visible rows by real availability before showing no-source rows.
  huggingface_review_conversion_label: Normal supported `.safetensors` source rows use `Start Conversion`; large, unknown-size, or GGUF source rows use `Review Conversion` with P2P-preferred warnings; rows without supported `.safetensors` or reviewable `.gguf` source metadata expose model-card review only and do not offer a conversion action.
  browser_generated_p2p_import_kit_exec: `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` chains the exact conversion kit into an explicit direct-peer import without catalog publication. It serves a peer-free base catalog plus manifest metadata, explicitly saves a consenting path-prefixed known-peer URL, and serves peer status, companion state, and pieces from that loopback peer. The browser writes the exact deny-unknown-fields `minimodel.peer_import_request.v0` schema; MiniModel inspects it before network access, validates status and receiver preflight before piece transfer, assembles and verifies the `.slm`, inspects the receipt chain, imports through the bounded Rust/WASM picker, and runs generation. Mapped-host and loopback results are local evidence only, never outside-network proof.
  browser_generated_p2p_import_receipt_reject: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js <app-url> <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 hf-p2p-import-receipt-reject` reuses the converted-once P2P setup, tampers the `.minimodel-receipt` artifact SHA-256 after Rust import/inspection, selects the peer-assembled `.slm` plus tampered receipt in the browser, and proves TinyRustLM reports `MiniModel import receipt artifact.sha256 mismatch` without selecting the local model or rendering `minimodel-p2p-import-receipt` provenance.
  local_import_ambiguous_selection_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js <app-url> <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 local-import-ambiguous-selection` proves the local file picker rejects more than one selected `.slm` file and more than one `.minimodel-receipt` sidecar before local model selection, preserving the previous model/provenance state instead of guessing which artifact to trust.
  browser_generated_p2p_import_request_inspector: The generated `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` script now runs MiniModel `inspect-peer-import-request` after request/manifest sidecars are ready and before `check-peer-status`; browser-smoke asserts `MiniModel peer import request validation: PASS` plus the no-network inspection message before any peer status/preflight/import work.
  browser_generated_peer_status_check_inspector: The generated `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` script now runs MiniModel `inspect-peer-status-check` after `check-peer-status` writes the saved JSON and before preflight; browser-smoke asserts `MiniModel peer status check validation: PASS` plus the saved-report inspection message before piece metadata moves.
  local_connect_full_mode_sync: Local Connect full local-control lab mode now preserves the rendered endpoint app inventory when the mode changes and immediately recomputes app-row decisions; `local-connect-endpoint-ui` asserts that terminal app rows become `allow` under full mode while explicitly blocked secrets-category rows remain `deny`.
  local_connect_action_category_binding: Local Connect `decide-approval`, `/v0/decision`, and `/v0/action` are category-bound; approved app names only authorize requests in their known category, browser-preview and real-endpoint smokes cover cross-category approved-app reuse staying `ask`, and Rust tests cover browser/email/path action dry-runs plus mismatched-category and unsafe-target rejection.
  local_connect_action_request_fingerprint: Local Connect `/v0/action` now returns `action_request_sha256`, CLI `execute-action` prints `action.request_sha256`, and browser validation plus mock/real endpoint smokes require a valid request fingerprint before trusting action dry-run evidence.
  local_connect_endpoint_contract_ids: Local Connect `/v0/health`, `/v0/apps`, `/v0/decision`, and `/v0/action` now advertise browser-enforced contract IDs for name-only app inventory (`app_inventory_policy=bounded-name-discovery-no-paths-v1`, `app_inventory_path_exposure=never`), category-bound app approvals (`app_approval_binding_policy=app-and-category-v1`), and dry-run-first typed action execution (`action_execution_policy=typed-action-dry-run-default-execution-consent-v1`); non-dry-run native-opener execution requires `x-tinyrustlm-execution-consent: native-opener-v1`, and Rust CLI/endpoint tests plus browser validation reject weaker endpoint shapes.
local_connect_policy_hot_reload: `tinyrustlm-local-connect serve-approval-endpoint <policy.json> [port]` now revalidates the watched policy file before each request, applies valid saved-policy replacements without restarting the endpoint, and returns fail-closed `policy-reload-failed` responses when the watched policy is missing or invalid; Rust CLI coverage mutates the policy from browser/category allow to ask and then to malformed JSON while the endpoint is running.
local_connect_rust_endpoint_hot_reload_smoke_2026_07_06: `node .\tinyrustlm\tools\browser-smoke.js http://127.0.0.1:8180/app/ 9331 tinylm16q8 local-connect-rust-endpoint-ui` passed against the source app served by `tinyrustlm-local-server`, and `node .\tinyrustlm\tools\browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:8181/ 9332 tinylm16q8 local-connect-rust-endpoint-ui` passed against the packaged TinyRustLM.com root through loopback host mapping; both runs proved real Rust `/v0/health`, `/v0/categories`, `/v0/apps`, `/v0/decision`, and `/v0/action` integration, category-bound app approvals, full local-control row recomputation, policy digest mismatch rejection, endpoint policy JSON export, and watched-policy-file status text without app execution.
nuget_readiness_fresh_report_guard_2026_07_06: `eng/audit-nuget-release-readiness.ps1` and `.sh` now clear each expected subreport path before running the publish-plan, local feed-current, local feed-hash, remote feed-current, or remote feed-hash step; the readiness report records `report_written` per step and also clears skipped remote-hash evidence, so stale JSON from an older release attempt cannot prove that the protected NuGet packages are current or publishable.
nuget_typed_wrapper_api_2026_07_06: The .NET NuGet SDK wrapper now exposes `TinyRustLmRuntimeFactory.GetVersion()` for native SDK/ABI diagnostics, typed `P2PShareKitReport` from `TinyRustLmP2PClient.PrepareLocalShareKit`, typed `P2PShareMetadata` from `ExportShareMetadata`, typed `P2PAnnouncement` / `P2PAnnouncementCatalog` records from announcement validation and catalog application, and explicit raw `PrepareLocalShareKitJson` / `ExportShareMetadataJson` / `ValidateAnnouncementJson` / `ApplyReceivedAnnouncementJson` methods for exact handoff JSON; Core tests and clean consumer smoke verify these typed records plus public P2P boundary flags.
  browser_generated_p2p_import_receipt_inspector: The generated `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` script now runs MiniModel `inspect-import-receipt` after `import-peer-request`; browser-smoke asserts `MiniModel import receipt validation: PASS` plus the receipt-inspection message before local browser import.
  peer_availability_refresh_preserves_hf_sources: Peer URL, peer contact card, and P2P toggle refreshes rerender accepted Hugging Face rows directly instead of re-normalizing them as raw API records, so `.safetensors` and `.gguf` sibling metadata, source byte counts, and `Start Conversion` / `Review Conversion` fallback actions survive after a `P2P Import` handoff or KnownPeerBaseUrl update.
  self_contained_peer_import_kit: Generated `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` scripts embed the exact `minimodel.peer_import_request.v0` JSON and recreate the sidecar if it is missing before running Rust `minimodel check-peer-status`, `inspect-peer-status-check`, `preflight-peer-import-request`, `import-peer-request`, and `inspect-import-receipt`; the script may fetch small MiniModel manifest metadata, validates peer status and advertised peer companion state when available, and fetches model pieces only from the consenting peer URL.
  self_contained_peer_import_kit_inspection: The self-contained script now inserts `minimodel inspect-peer-import-request <request-json> <manifest>` before peer network access, so request/manifest drift and project-server-byte boundary failures stop locally.
  known_peer_conversion_kit: When P2P is enabled and the user sets `Known peer URL`, the generated script may write only local peer-companion, contact-card/book, and companion-inventory handoff metadata for that consenting peer. The base catalog remains peer-free. The script cannot create an announcement and prints `prepare-seed-announcement` only as the later step after external probe, observer trust, and fleet inputs exist.
  conversion_readme_kit: Hugging Face `Start Conversion` downloads a three-file local kit: request JSON, self-contained PowerShell script, and a beginner README that explains reviewed `.safetensors` placement, local Rust conversion, MiniModel peer-share outputs, safe metadata publication, and files that must never be uploaded to project servers.
  empty_announcement_feed_rule: A checksum-bound peer-source announcement feed with a valid metadata-only envelope and empty `announcements` array is a valid availability check; TinyRustLM must report the feed check and leave proof-ready rows at `Set Peer URL` until a matching announcement names a real consenting peer.
  public_site_boundary: TinyRustLM.com is a pre-release browser-local product surface. It loads app/runtime assets, waits for an explicit local file or consenting direct peer, and never obtains model bytes from project servers. Local picker input uses bounded slices and Rust-owned digest finalization before runtime adoption. Hugging Face remains metadata discovery plus a local conversion handoff. Conversion/share scripts produce peer pieces, a peer-free base catalog, local receipts, and optional consenting companion/contact metadata; they do not generate announcements. A direct import request contains only MiniModel's exact strict schema, and the operational commands remain in the generated script. Catalog announcement input is accepted only through the current external-proof verifier. Loopback, mapped-host, and local companion tests remain pre-release local evidence and cannot support a public-reachability or live-release claim.
  public_live_smoke_rule: `tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js` maps TinyRustLM public hostnames to loopback for local `http://tinyrustlm.com:PORT/` simulations and treats that mapped origin as secure so file-import SHA-256 checks can run; live `https://tinyrustlm.com/` checks must use real DNS and prove only app/runtime assets load before user action.
  public_host_local_import_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/ <cdp-port> tinyq8 catalog-local-import` can now exercise the root-domain public-host branch locally, import a real user-selected fixture `.slm`, verify SHA-256/provenance, run Rust/WASM generation, and make only app/runtime network requests before the local file is selected.
  public_host_local_import_ambiguous_selection_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/ <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 local-import-ambiguous-selection` proves the root-domain package fails closed on duplicate `.slm` and duplicate receipt selections without project-served model bytes or local model selection.
  public_host_peer_url_unsafe_smoke: `node tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/ <cdp-port> tinylm16q8 peer-url-unsafe-ui` proves the root-domain package rejects unsafe Known peer URLs, including project/Hugging Face root-dot and subdomain host variants, before request/script generation while accepting the normal path-prefixed loopback MiniModel peer URL.
local_share_kit_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-local-share-kit-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: After Rust/WASM verifies a local `.slm`, TinyRustLM can save a metadata-only `minimodel.local_slm_share_metadata.v0` bundle and a separate share-kit-ready bundle with direct MiniModel peer protocol hints while `network_transfer_available=false` until the user runs local scripts with a consenting peer URL. The paired scripts verify artifact byte count/SHA-256, run `prepare-peer-share`, write a peer-free catalog and local receipt ledger, and may write peer-companion state, contact card/book, and inventory handoffs. They contain no announcement/feed, with-peer catalog, or unproven publication path and print only the later proof-gated `prepare-seed-announcement` command shape.
  browser_generated_share_metadata_kit_exec: `share-metadata-kit-exec` executes the exact browser-downloaded local share kit with a consenting loopback peer URL, verifies the manifest, peer offer, peer-free catalog, local receipt ledger, companion state, contact card/book, inventory, current inspector PASS output, and absence of removed announcement/feed commands. It starts local companion serving only after state inspection and treats mapped-host results as local evidence, not public proof.
  public_root_share_metadata_kit_exec: The same `share-metadata-kit-exec` smoke is green against the packaged TinyRustLM.com root through mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/`, proving public-host assets can import a verified local `.slm`, save the P2P share kit, execute the exact downloaded scripts, start local companion serving, and validate peer-status metadata without project-hosted model bytes.
  local_peer_announcement_feed_import: `hf-peer-announcement-ui` loads a local catalog envelope containing a current version-1 complete-transfer announcement fixture and proves parser/routing behavior from source and mapped root assets. Rejection smokes cover duplicate rows, stale or sampled proof, identity drift, route-count drift, and oversized metadata. These fixtures do not count as outside-network proof.
  boundary: The share kit never uploads `.slm` bytes or peer pieces to TinyRustLM.com, MiniModel.org, or any project server; catalog maintainers receive only metadata JSON.
huggingface_real_conversion_script_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-real-conversion-script-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: `Start Conversion` now reports `Rust conversion script saved`; the generated `.tinyrustlm-convert.ps1` script discovers the Rust-produced `.slm` and conversion receipt after `convert-huggingface-request`, then discovers the MiniModel manifest, catalog entry, peer-piece directory, and optional peer-companion state after `prepare-peer-share` instead of guessing filenames, and writes a local `.minimodel-serve-peer-pieces.ps1` helper that re-inspects companion state with `inspect-peer-companion-state` before preferring `serve-peer-companion` when state exists.
  boundary: Hugging Face remains metadata/source discovery only; project servers still never fetch, run, proxy, host, or serve user model bytes.
huggingface_self_contained_conversion_script_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-self-contained-conversion-script-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: `Start Conversion` still saves a visible request JSON, but the generated `.tinyrustlm-convert.ps1` also embeds that request as base64, writes it beside the script if the JSON sidecar is missing, and embeds the local peer-serving helper it writes into the conversion output directory.
  boundary: The generated script remains local-only, requires a user-owned `.safetensors`, and keeps conversion, validation, share metadata, and catalog snapshot work in local Rust commands.
huggingface_conversion_receipt_p2p_hints_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-conversion-receipt-p2p-hints-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: This dated receipt-hints design is superseded. Current version-2 receipts include the local share directory, `prepare-peer-share`, peer-free catalog, local companion/contact commands, peer-piece serving, and the later external-proof-only `prepare-seed-announcement` shape. They contain no unproven announcement/feed command.
  boundary: The receipt remains proof and guidance only; it does not fetch Hugging Face bytes, upload `.slm` files, start peer serving, or make project servers host model bytes.
huggingface_conversion_publish_feed_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-conversion-publish-feed-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: This dated publication flow is superseded and unsupported. Current scripts turn a known consenting peer URL only into local companion/contact/inventory handoffs and a peer-free catalog; public announcement requires the separate complete-transfer-proof gate.
  boundary: The package contains publication guidance and JSON metadata only; the converter still keeps `.slm` files and peer-piece directories local and serves pieces only from a user-run peer endpoint.
converted_once_p2p_smoke_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-converted-once-p2p-smoke-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: This dated workflow is superseded. The current smoke runs local fixture -> TinyRustLM conversion -> MiniModel peer-share -> peer-free catalog plus local companion/contact/inventory handoffs and asserts that no announcement/feed is created.
  boundary: The smoke asserts metadata-only publication fields and rejects artifact/model URLs, Hugging Face `/resolve/`, and project-hosted `/models/` byte routes.
self_contained_peer_import_kit_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-self-contained-peer-import-kit-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: Browser-generated P2P import scripts now embed and can recreate their peer-import request JSON before running MiniModel `check-peer-status`, `inspect-peer-status-check`, `preflight-peer-import-request`, and `import-peer-request`.
  behavior: Browser-generated P2P import scripts now also run MiniModel `inspect-peer-import-request` before `check-peer-status`, giving a no-network request/manifest validation gate.
  behavior: Browser-generated P2P import scripts now also run MiniModel `inspect-import-receipt` after import, giving a local receipt/artifact revalidation gate before browser import.
  boundary: The script still does not fetch model bytes from project servers or Hugging Face; model pieces come only from the consenting peer URL and are reverified by Rust.
known_peer_conversion_kit_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-known-peer-conversion-kit-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: Browser-generated Hugging Face conversion requests/scripts now carry the list-level Known peer URL into `known_peer_base_url` and `$KnownPeerBaseUrl` when P2P is enabled.
  boundary: The peer URL is consent metadata for local MiniModel peer-source publication only; project servers still never fetch, serve, proxy, cache, or run model bytes.
conversion_readme_kit_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-conversion-readme-kit-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: Browser-generated Hugging Face conversion kits now save request JSON, `.tinyrustlm-convert.ps1`, and `.tinyrustlm-conversion.README.txt` so beginners get the local source-file, conversion, import, safe-publication, and no-server-byte instructions beside the runnable script.
  boundary: The README keeps Hugging Face as metadata-only discovery and says never to upload `.slm`, peer-piece, or source `.safetensors` files to project servers.
browser_generated_conversion_kit_exec_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-browser-generated-conversion-kit-exec-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: This dated route is superseded by the independent safetensors, reviewed-shard, GGUF, and review-reject modes in `current_local_import_and_p2p_authority_2026_07_15`. Current success paths produce a peer-free base catalog and local handoff metadata; they do not create announcement feeds.
  fail_closed_behavior: The targeted review-reject smoke proves Rust preflight reports `source_contract_status=fail` and `conversion_decision=source-contract-rejected-before-conversion`, then verifies no `.slm`, receipt, or MiniModel peer-share output is produced.
  boundary: The execution proof still uses only local files and metadata publication JSON; project servers never receive `.slm`, peer-piece, or source `.safetensors` bytes.
browser_generated_p2p_import_kit_exec_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-browser-generated-p2p-import-kit-exec-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: The current `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` smoke uses a peer-free base catalog, explicit known-peer selection, an exact strict MiniModel request, receiver preflight, receipt-chain validation, bounded local browser import, and Rust/WASM generation. It does not consume or generate an unproven announcement feed, and its mapped-host result is not public reachability evidence.
  boundary: Later-user import downloads only small catalog/manifest metadata from the catalog endpoint and fetches model bytes only from consenting `http://127.0.0.1:8123/` peer pieces; project and Hugging Face hosts do not provide model bytes, and the 2026-07-03 intake keeps desktop companion work as a later optional wrapper around the same Rust verifier.
gguf_q8_0_conversion_gate_2026_07_05:
  route: tinyrustlm/tools/slm_pack/src/gguf.rs
  behavior: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack inspect-gguf <input.gguf> [output.report]` streams GGUF metadata and tensor-directory bytes, validates version, alignment, supported GGML tensor encodings, byte ranges, and overlap-free tensor spans, and writes checksum-bearing report rows; `plan-gguf-source`, `extract-gguf-source`, and `convert-gguf-trained` map supported F32/F16/BF16/Q2_K/Q3_K/Q4_0/Q4_1/Q4_K/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0/Q8_1/Q8_K GGUF tensors into the raw f32 trained-source layout and then into f32/q8_0/q4_0 `.slm`; `write-gguf-fixture`, `write-gguf-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q8-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q8-1-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q8-k-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q2-k-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q3-k-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q6-k-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q4-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q4-1-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q4-k-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q5-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q5-1-source-fixture`, `write-gguf-q5-k-source-fixture`, Rust unit tests, and public CLI tests cover deterministic inspection, planning, raw-source extraction, quantized dequantization, and f32/q8/q4 `.slm` conversion from reviewed GGUF sources, plus unaligned-offset, overlap, unsupported-type, and tokenizer-boundary rejection.
  boundary: GGUF conversion still requires supported tensor names/shapes, tokenizer token-count compatibility, and Rust validation before `.slm` import; unsupported tensor encodings and incompatible source shapes fail closed before output artifacts are trusted.
huggingface_sharded_source_directory_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-sharded-source-directory-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: Browser Hugging Face source metadata and Rust conversion now support a reviewed single `.safetensors` file or reviewed shard directory; inspect/plan/preflight/receipt evidence records `source_file_count` plus per-tensor source paths.
  boundary: Hugging Face search remains metadata-only, local scripts download directly from Hugging Face only after explicit opt-in, and project servers still never host, proxy, cache, run, or serve user model bytes.
huggingface_availability_summary_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-availability-summary-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: The simple Hugging Face panel now shows `Model availability` chips for `P2P Import`, `Set Peer URL`, `Start Conversion`, `Review First`, `Local .slm`, `No Source`, and `P2P Off` from the same view model that renders row actions.
  boundary: The chips are metadata UX only; a model runs only after local Rust conversion creates a `.slm` or a consenting peer transfer is assembled and reverified by Rust.
simple_local_catalog_prioritized_hf_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-simple-local-catalog-prioritized-hf-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: The beginner P2P source panel can load a local `models.v0.json` snapshot, while Hugging Face search fetches a wider metadata page and ranks visible rows by P2P-ready, proof-ready, local `.slm`, source-backed conversion, review, and no-source actionability.
  boundary: The feature remains metadata-only; model bytes still enter only through user-selected local files, reviewed local conversion sources, or consenting peer pieces reverified by Rust.
huggingface_review_conversion_label_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-huggingface-source-size-risk-memory-2026-07-03.md
  behavior: Large or unknown-size Hugging Face source rows now say `Review Conversion`, not `Prepare Conversion`, so the beginner UI makes the review gate explicit while normal source-backed rows still save the real conversion kit with `Start Conversion`.
  boundary: `Review Conversion` is still metadata/handoff UI only; model bytes move only through user-owned local sources or consenting peer imports reverified by Rust.
desktop_p2p_companion_2026_07_03:
  route: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-desktop-p2p-companion-intake-memory-2026-07-03.md
  intake: docs/report-intake/2026-07-03/MANIFEST.md
  guidance: Six desktop/P2P reports support a later optional user-run MiniModel Peer Companion for local piece storage, peer identity, consent prompts, cache quotas, direct serve/fetch controls, and import receipts; the current browser app stays the simple local `.slm` path and project servers still never host, proxy, cache, run, or serve user model bytes.
deploy_gate:
  instruction: Before every TinyRustLM deploy or SLMComposer.com retirement/redirect change, update the related documentation sites and public-safe exports so live docs match the app behavior being deployed.
  related_documentation_sites:
    - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com
    - MiniModel.org
    - MiniModel.MiRust.com
    - MiRust.com
  requirements:
    - Keep source-control folders as the deploy source of truth; do not deploy stale archived publish copies by accident.
    - Update workspace.uai and affected .uai/public talisman exports when boundaries, live behavior, deployment access, source options, or verification claims change.
    - Run relevant pointer audits and git diff --check before packaging or deployment.
    - If deployment access is missing or live docs cannot be updated, record the blocker and do not claim the site is deployed.
active_intake_state:
  scanned_utc: 2026-08-09T00:53:15Z
  status: placeholder_only_after_exact_active_handoff_closure
  content_bucket_non_placeholder_files: 0
  improvement_bucket_non_placeholder_files: 0
  instruction: Six remaining source artifacts were preserved exactly under docs/report-intake/2026-08-08/active-handoff-closure/, synthesized into durable memory, routed into goal and blocker state, and removed from active intake after hash verification. The enterprise goal remains active through the goal system and durable memory; external MemoryEndpoints and future compressed-vector work must not be represented by leaving processed files in intake.
memory_authority:
  hot_memory_root: .uai/
  llm_wiki_namespace: wiki/runtime-mirust/
  aiwikis_public_namespace: https://aiwikis.org/runtime-mirust/
  file_handoff_root: agent-file-handoff/
  site_voice_hot_memory: .uai/taboo.uai
  split_memory_architecture_rule: Hot `.uai` files remain active startup/current-state/operational memory even when durable wiki/docs memory exists; durable memory augments `.uai`, and agents must not retire, ignore, or make `.uai` emergency-only because long-term memory is available.
  uaix_file_handoff_strategy_source: https://uaix.org/en-us/tools/ai-memory-package-wizard/#setup-file-handoff
  report_storage_strategy: hot_uai_routes_current_state_and_synthesis; durable_reports_live_in_wiki_raw_evidence_and_pointer_ledgers
  research_reference_strategy: diverse_model_breeding_reference_bodies_live_in_wiki_research_and_route_through_short_term_memory_report_synthesis_and_long_term_checksum_pointers; lanes include compatible_merge_dare_dropout_rescaled_task_delta_sparse_lineage_adapter_ecology_with_trained_source_alr1_and_adp1_asp1_alr1_population_search_federated_local_update_browser_constrained_assembly_uaix_memory_strategy_heritable_artifacts_mate_selection_phenotype_evidence_speciation_fit_genome_fitness_novelty_and_zero_dependency_browser_runtime_guidance
